1
00:03:05,060 --> 00:03:08,063
LOUIS : So you want me to tell you the story of my life .

2
00:03:08,188 --> 00:03:11,567
INTERVIEWER : Like I said , that 's what I do . I interview people .

3
00:03:11,692 --> 00:03:13,235
I 'm a collector of lives .

4
00:03:13,318 --> 00:03:15,070
FM radio , KFRC .

5
00:03:15,237 --> 00:03:17,823
LOUIS : You 'll need a lot of tape for my story .

6
00:03:17,948 --> 00:03:20,492
No problem . I got a bag full of tape .

7
00:03:21,743 --> 00:03:24,246
LOUIS : You followed me here , didn 't you ?

8
00:03:24,496 --> 00:03:26,456
Yeah , I suppose I did .

9
00:03:26,957 --> 00:03:28,834
You seemed very interesting .

10
00:03:30,002 --> 00:03:31,753
This is where you live ?

11
00:03:32,212 --> 00:03:33,255
LOUIS : No .

12
00:03:33,338 --> 00:03:34,965
It 's just a room .

13
00:03:37,509 --> 00:03:40,387
INTERVIEWER : What do you say we get started ?

14
00:03:42,764 --> 00:03:44,266
What do you do ?

15
00:03:44,474 --> 00:03:45,976
LOUIS : I 'm a vampire .

16
00:03:48,729 --> 00:03:51,106
[ Chuckling ] I haven 't heard that before .

17
00:03:51,523 --> 00:03:53,859
You mean this literally , I take it ?

18
00:03:54,026 --> 00:03:55,485
LOUIS : Absolutely .

19
00:03:56,278 --> 00:03:58,614
I was waiting for you in that alley .

20
00:03:58,864 --> 00:04:01,033
Watching you watching me .

21
00:04:01,992 --> 00:04:03,869
And then you began to speak .

22
00:04:04,870 --> 00:04:07,039
What a lucky break for me .

23
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:09,499
LOUIS : Perhaps lucky for both of us .

24
00:04:13,045 --> 00:04:15,255
INTERVIEWER : You said you were

25
00:04:15,380 --> 00:04:17,049
waiting for me .

26
00:04:17,508 --> 00:04:20,761
What were you going to do ? Kill me , drink my blood ?

27
00:04:20,844 --> 00:04:22,012
LOUIS : Yes .

28
00:04:22,930 --> 00:04:25,140
But you needn 't be concerned now .

29
00:04:27,559 --> 00:04:31,522
INTERVIEWER : You really believe this , don 't you , that you 're a vampire ?

30
00:04:31,647 --> 00:04:33,565
We can 't begin this way .

31
00:04:33,774 --> 00:04:35,442
Let me turn on the light .

32
00:04:36,276 --> 00:04:39,571
- I thought vampires didn 't like light . - We love it .

33
00:04:40,906 --> 00:04:43,158
I only wanted to prepare you .

34
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:45,410
[ Loud effect when light turned on ]

35
00:04:45,536 --> 00:04:46,453
Christ !

36
00:04:46,578 --> 00:04:48,330
Don 't be frightened .

37
00:04:48,956 --> 00:04:51,041
I want this opportunity .

38
00:04:51,083 --> 00:04:53,293
INTERVIEWER : How the hell did you do that ?

39
00:04:53,293 --> 00:04:55,128
LOUIS : The same as you do .

40
00:04:55,546 --> 00:04:57,923
A series of simple gestures .

41
00:04:58,090 --> 00:05:00,467
Only I moved too fast for you to see .

42
00:05:01,844 --> 00:05:03,428
I 'm flesh and blood

43
00:05:03,595 --> 00:05:05,180
but not human .

44
00:05:05,681 --> 00:05:08,809
I haven 't been human for 200 years .

45
00:05:10,686 --> 00:05:11,854
Please ...

46
00:05:20,362 --> 00:05:22,364
How can I put you at ease ?

47
00:05:22,823 --> 00:05:25,367
Shall we begin like " David Copperfield " ?

48
00:05:25,492 --> 00:05:26,660
" I am born ...

49
00:05:26,827 --> 00:05:28,078
" ... I grew up . "

50
00:05:29,955 --> 00:05:34,334
Or shall we begin when I was born to darkness , as I call it .

51
00:05:35,836 --> 00:05:38,881
LOUIS : That 's where we should start , don 't you think ?

52
00:05:40,632 --> 00:05:42,634
You 're not lying , are you ?

53
00:05:43,719 --> 00:05:45,387
LOUIS : Why should I lie ?

54
00:05:47,389 --> 00:05:49,766
LOUIS : 1791 was the year it happened .

55
00:05:54,855 --> 00:05:56,607
I was 24 .

56
00:05:56,732 --> 00:05:58,859
Younger than you are now .

57
00:05:59,276 --> 00:06:02,613
But times were different then . I was a man at that age .

58
00:06:02,696 --> 00:06:06,867
The master of a large plantation , just south of New Orleans .

59
00:06:10,120 --> 00:06:12,623
I had lost my wife in childbirth .

60
00:06:12,706 --> 00:06:16,001
She and the infant had been buried less than half a year .

61
00:06:17,127 --> 00:06:19,296
I would 've been happy to join them .

62
00:06:21,757 --> 00:06:24,384
I couldn 't bear the pain of their loss .

63
00:06:24,676 --> 00:06:27,137
I longed to be released from it .

64
00:06:28,388 --> 00:06:30,390
[ Horse neighs , crickets chirp ]

65
00:06:37,189 --> 00:06:39,566
[ Scattered voices , ambient bar noise ]

66
00:06:39,900 --> 00:06:41,902
LOUIS : I wanted to lose it all :

67
00:06:42,027 --> 00:06:43,529
my wealth

68
00:06:44,196 --> 00:06:45,656
my estate

69
00:06:46,198 --> 00:06:47,783
my sanity .

70
00:06:56,041 --> 00:06:57,960
How many aces are in a deck ?

71
00:06:58,418 --> 00:07:00,212
Are you calling me a cheat ?

72
00:07:03,215 --> 00:07:06,426
GAMBLER : No , I 'm calling you a piece of stinking offal !

73
00:07:08,303 --> 00:07:09,847
[ Rifle clicks ]

74
00:07:11,807 --> 00:07:14,685
You lack the courage of your convictions . Do it !

75
00:07:15,310 --> 00:07:18,188
LOUIS : Most of all , I longed for death .

76
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:20,065
I know that now .

77
00:07:20,732 --> 00:07:22,442
I invited it .

78
00:07:23,318 --> 00:07:25,946
A release from the pain of living .

79
00:07:31,535 --> 00:07:34,121
[ Scattered conversations and laughter ]

80
00:07:47,217 --> 00:07:49,845
LOUIS : My invitation was open to anyone .

81
00:07:50,596 --> 00:07:52,764
To the whore at my side .

82
00:07:53,765 --> 00:07:55,976
To the pimp that followed .

83
00:07:58,103 --> 00:08:01,106
But it was a vampire that accepted .

84
00:08:27,508 --> 00:08:29,801
THIEF : Give me your money or you die !

85
00:08:32,763 --> 00:08:33,805
[ Screaming ]

86
00:08:33,889 --> 00:08:36,016
[ Sound of neck cracking ]

87
00:08:39,561 --> 00:08:41,522
[ Lestat hisses ]

88
00:08:50,155 --> 00:08:52,699
[ Dramatic , high-pitched instrumental music ]

89
00:09:04,169 --> 00:09:06,171
LESTAT : Do you still want death ?

90
00:09:06,296 --> 00:09:08,340
Or have you tasted it enough ?

91
00:09:08,465 --> 00:09:09,800
LOUIS : Enough .

92
00:09:19,226 --> 00:09:22,646
LOUIS : He left me there , on the banks of the Mississippi

93
00:09:23,564 --> 00:09:26,608
somewhere between life and death .

94
00:09:34,825 --> 00:09:36,368
[ Coughing ]

95
00:09:43,709 --> 00:09:44,960
[ Rifle clicks ]

96
00:09:45,085 --> 00:09:47,713
Who are you ? What 're you doing in my house ?

97
00:09:48,589 --> 00:09:51,216
LESTAT : I 've come to answer your prayers .

98
00:09:53,719 --> 00:09:56,430
LESTAT : Life has no meaning anymore ... does it ?

99
00:10:00,100 --> 00:10:02,269
The wine has no taste .

100
00:10:02,436 --> 00:10:04,396
The food sickens you .

101
00:10:04,521 --> 00:10:07,524
There seems no reason for any of it ... does there ?

102
00:10:12,613 --> 00:10:15,115
What if I could give it back to you ?

103
00:10:15,407 --> 00:10:16,992
Pluck out the pain

104
00:10:17,117 --> 00:10:19,119
and give you another life ?

105
00:10:19,745 --> 00:10:22,122
One you could never imagine .

106
00:10:23,165 --> 00:10:25,250
And it would be ... for all time .

107
00:10:27,628 --> 00:10:28,962
And sickness

108
00:10:29,129 --> 00:10:30,631
and death

109
00:10:30,756 --> 00:10:33,133
could never touch you again .

110
00:10:34,801 --> 00:10:36,303
Don 't be afraid .

111
00:10:37,137 --> 00:10:39,640
I 'm going to give you the choice

112
00:10:39,765 --> 00:10:40,766
I

113
00:10:41,141 --> 00:10:42,559
never had .

114
00:10:51,944 --> 00:10:54,696
LOUIS : That morning , I was not yet a vampire

115
00:10:54,821 --> 00:10:57,658
and I saw my last sunrise .

116
00:10:58,325 --> 00:11:00,661
I remember it completely

117
00:11:01,286 --> 00:11:04,665
and yet I can 't recall any sunrise before it .

118
00:11:06,959 --> 00:11:10,587
I watched the whole magnificence of the dawn for the last time

119
00:11:10,796 --> 00:11:12,673
as if it were the first .

120
00:11:16,677 --> 00:11:19,304
And then I said farewell to sunlight

121
00:11:19,346 --> 00:11:21,431
and set out to become

122
00:11:21,515 --> 00:11:22,516
what I became .

123
00:11:24,476 --> 00:11:26,687
[ Crickets chirp ]

124
00:11:29,606 --> 00:11:31,191
[ Loon cries ]

125
00:11:43,203 --> 00:11:46,081
LESTAT : Have you said your good-byes to the light ?

126
00:11:47,457 --> 00:11:49,626
[ Louis gasps and screams ]

127
00:12:08,353 --> 00:12:09,980
LESTAT : I 've drained you

128
00:12:10,063 --> 00:12:12,232
to the point of death .

129
00:12:13,358 --> 00:12:15,402
If I leave you here

130
00:12:15,569 --> 00:12:16,904
you 'll die .

131
00:12:18,071 --> 00:12:18,989
Or

132
00:12:20,073 --> 00:12:23,243
you can be young always , my friend

133
00:12:24,411 --> 00:12:26,246
as we are now .

134
00:12:27,748 --> 00:12:29,750
But you must tell me

135
00:12:30,250 --> 00:12:31,668
will you come

136
00:12:31,752 --> 00:12:32,878
or no ?

137
00:12:36,757 --> 00:12:38,050
LOUIS : Yes .

138
00:12:43,430 --> 00:12:44,765
Yes .

139
00:13:13,961 --> 00:13:16,547
[ Heavy breathing and grunting ]

140
00:13:16,588 --> 00:13:20,133
[ Simulated heartbeat , background ]

141
00:13:31,687 --> 00:13:33,856
[ Wailing and choking ]

142
00:13:48,120 --> 00:13:49,997
LESTAT : Your body 's dying .

143
00:13:50,330 --> 00:13:51,957
Pay no attention .

144
00:13:52,624 --> 00:13:54,501
It happens to us all .

145
00:13:56,920 --> 00:13:58,881
[ Louis gasps ]

146
00:14:04,011 --> 00:14:06,180
[ Lestat sighs ]

147
00:14:24,656 --> 00:14:25,782
LESTAT : Now look

148
00:14:25,866 --> 00:14:28,160
with your vampire eyes .

149
00:14:46,720 --> 00:14:48,180
What did you see ?

150
00:14:49,056 --> 00:14:51,183
LOUIS : No words can describe it .

151
00:14:52,893 --> 00:14:55,395
Might as well ask Heaven what it sees .

152
00:14:55,521 --> 00:14:57,231
No human can know .

153
00:14:58,732 --> 00:15:01,401
LOUIS : The statue seemed to move , but didn 't .

154
00:15:01,902 --> 00:15:04,905
The world had changed , yet stayed the same .

155
00:15:06,198 --> 00:15:10,160
I was a newborn vampire , weeping at the beauty of the night .

156
00:15:15,916 --> 00:15:18,544
LOUIS : Perhaps you 'd like another cigarette ?

157
00:15:19,503 --> 00:15:22,256
INTERVIEWER : I would . It 's not bothering you , is it ?

158
00:15:22,422 --> 00:15:26,343
I don 't assume it would . It 's not like you 'll die from cancer .

159
00:15:27,052 --> 00:15:28,679
I don 't think so .

160
00:15:30,347 --> 00:15:33,183
INTERVIEWER : What about crucifixes ? LOUIS : Crucifixes ?

161
00:15:33,267 --> 00:15:35,185
Can you look at them ?

162
00:15:35,352 --> 00:15:38,313
Actually , I 'm quite fond of looking at crucifixes .

163
00:15:39,189 --> 00:15:41,275
And the stake through the heart ?

164
00:15:41,441 --> 00:15:42,609
LOUIS : Nonsense .

165
00:15:42,693 --> 00:15:43,944
And coffins ?

166
00:15:44,945 --> 00:15:46,321
Coffins .

167
00:15:46,363 --> 00:15:49,074
Coffins , unfortunately , are a necessity .

168
00:15:51,743 --> 00:15:53,787
LESTAT : [ Whispering ] Don 't worry .

169
00:15:54,079 --> 00:15:55,247
Soon

170
00:15:55,789 --> 00:15:59,209
you 'll be sleeping as soundly as you 've ever slept .

171
00:16:00,961 --> 00:16:02,796
And when you awake

172
00:16:03,797 --> 00:16:05,716
I 'll be waiting for you

173
00:16:06,550 --> 00:16:09,094
and so will all the world .

174
00:16:16,393 --> 00:16:17,644
[ Violin playing period music ]

175
00:16:17,728 --> 00:16:21,106
LOUIS : Blood , I was to find , was a necessity as well .

176
00:16:22,107 --> 00:16:25,986
I awoke the next evening with a hunger I had never felt .

177
00:16:27,613 --> 00:16:29,740
WOMAN : Once you taste this

178
00:16:29,907 --> 00:16:33,076
you 'll never go to another tavern again .

179
00:16:33,577 --> 00:16:35,245
LESTAT : You think so ?

180
00:16:36,246 --> 00:16:39,291
But what if I 'd rather taste your lips ?

181
00:16:39,833 --> 00:16:42,419
My lips are even sweeter still .

182
00:16:48,759 --> 00:16:50,761
[ Heavy breathing ]

183
00:16:52,888 --> 00:16:54,431
[ Woman moans ]

184
00:16:57,851 --> 00:16:59,645
My friend

185
00:17:00,145 --> 00:17:02,356
should taste those lips .

186
00:17:02,523 --> 00:17:04,066
WOMAN : [ Trembling ] Is his

187
00:17:04,149 --> 00:17:05,317
kiss

188
00:17:05,526 --> 00:17:06,693
as deep

189
00:17:06,777 --> 00:17:08,278
as yours ?

190
00:17:09,530 --> 00:17:11,323
LESTAT : Deeper , ma chérie .

191
00:17:16,036 --> 00:17:19,456
[ Violin playing , talking and laughter , background ]

192
00:17:21,875 --> 00:17:23,627
[ Heavy breathing ]

193
00:17:42,813 --> 00:17:44,565
[ Louis gasps ]

194
00:17:44,648 --> 00:17:46,817
I will not take her life .

195
00:17:47,985 --> 00:17:49,695
I 've done it for you .

196
00:17:52,573 --> 00:17:54,867
[ Panting ] She 's dead

197
00:17:55,075 --> 00:17:57,369
as a doornail , my friend .

198
00:18:04,585 --> 00:18:07,880
LESTAT : It 's so easy , you almost feel sorry for them .

199
00:18:14,595 --> 00:18:16,221
You 'll get used to killing .

200
00:18:16,346 --> 00:18:18,974
Just forget about that mortal coil .

201
00:18:19,600 --> 00:18:22,394
You 'll become accustomed to it , all too quickly .

202
00:18:30,360 --> 00:18:31,862
Are you not hungry ?

203
00:18:31,904 --> 00:18:33,655
LESTAT : Au contraire , ma chérie .

204
00:18:33,739 --> 00:18:35,741
He could eat the whole colony .

205
00:18:35,866 --> 00:18:38,202
[ Lestat laughs hysterically ]

206
00:18:44,458 --> 00:18:46,210
[ Yvette gasps ]

207
00:18:54,635 --> 00:18:55,886
I will finish it .

208
00:18:55,886 --> 00:18:57,638
LOUIS : Now leave us .

209
00:19:05,145 --> 00:19:07,397
LESTAT : Can 't you pretend , you fool ?

210
00:19:07,523 --> 00:19:09,691
Don 't give the game away .

211
00:19:09,900 --> 00:19:12,194
We 're lucky to have such a home .

212
00:19:21,954 --> 00:19:24,456
Pretend to drink , at least .

213
00:19:29,294 --> 00:19:31,964
Such fine crystal shouldn 't go to waste .

214
00:19:53,193 --> 00:19:54,444
LESTAT : I know .

215
00:19:54,695 --> 00:19:56,697
It gets cold so quickly .

216
00:19:56,989 --> 00:19:58,574
LOUIS : We can live like this ?

217
00:19:58,699 --> 00:20:00,200
On animal blood ?

218
00:20:00,325 --> 00:20:03,495
I wouldn 't call it living . Call it surviving .

219
00:20:03,996 --> 00:20:06,748
Useful trick if you 're on a ship for a month .

220
00:20:09,376 --> 00:20:12,462
There 's nothing in the world now that doesn 't hold some ...

221
00:20:12,504 --> 00:20:13,839
Fascination .

222
00:20:14,965 --> 00:20:15,966
Yes .

223
00:20:16,967 --> 00:20:20,345
LESTAT : I 'm bored with this prattle . LOUIS : We can live without killing .

224
00:20:20,470 --> 00:20:21,722
It 's possible .

225
00:20:21,972 --> 00:20:23,473
Anything is possible .

226
00:20:23,515 --> 00:20:25,517
But just try it for a week .

227
00:20:25,976 --> 00:20:30,480
Come into New Orleans and let me show you some real sport .

228
00:20:33,650 --> 00:20:35,819
[ Orchestral music plays ]

229
00:20:40,616 --> 00:20:43,994
LOUIS : Lestat killed two , sometimes three a night .

230
00:20:44,786 --> 00:20:46,538
A fresh young girl

231
00:20:46,747 --> 00:20:49,583
was his favorite for the first of the evening .

232
00:20:50,292 --> 00:20:53,795
For seconds , he preferred a gilded , beautiful youth .

233
00:20:55,380 --> 00:20:58,800
But the snob in him loved to hunt in society .

234
00:20:59,510 --> 00:21:02,596
The blood of the aristocrat thrilled him best of all .

235
00:21:03,764 --> 00:21:06,391
The trick is not to think about it .

236
00:21:06,767 --> 00:21:08,143
You see that one ?

237
00:21:08,268 --> 00:21:09,770
Widow St. Clair .

238
00:21:10,020 --> 00:21:14,066
LESTAT : She had that gorgeous young fop murder her husband .

239
00:21:14,525 --> 00:21:16,193
LOUIS : How do you know ?

240
00:21:17,277 --> 00:21:18,820
Read her thoughts .

241
00:21:21,073 --> 00:21:22,824
Read her thoughts .

242
00:21:28,664 --> 00:21:30,040
I can 't .

243
00:21:31,792 --> 00:21:34,419
The " dark gift " is different for each of us .

244
00:21:34,795 --> 00:21:38,924
But one thing is true of everyone . We grow stronger as we go along .

245
00:21:39,842 --> 00:21:41,844
Just take my word for it .

246
00:21:42,928 --> 00:21:45,556
She blamed a slave for his murder .

247
00:21:45,681 --> 00:21:48,058
LESTAT : Imagine what they did to him .

248
00:21:48,559 --> 00:21:51,603
Evil-doers are easier , and they taste better .

249
00:21:51,687 --> 00:21:54,481
WIDOW ST . CLAIR : Enchantée , monsieur .

250
00:21:57,484 --> 00:21:58,819
Enchantée .

251
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:14,585
[ Dog barks ]

252
00:22:23,635 --> 00:22:25,345
MAN : Where are we going ?

253
00:22:32,686 --> 00:22:33,896
Nowhere .

254
00:22:34,980 --> 00:22:38,150
Now , young man , you really amaze me !

255
00:22:40,903 --> 00:22:44,156
I 'm old enough to be your grandmother .

256
00:22:52,414 --> 00:22:54,625
[ Widow St. Clair moans ]

257
00:22:58,378 --> 00:23:00,756
Oh , yes , that 's the melody .

258
00:23:01,256 --> 00:23:02,925
I remember it .

259
00:23:03,008 --> 00:23:05,636
[ Classical music plays , background ]

260
00:23:05,636 --> 00:23:08,263
[ Dogs continue barking and growling ]

261
00:23:14,937 --> 00:23:16,939
WIDOW ST . CLAIR : [ Screaming ] Murderer !

262
00:23:17,022 --> 00:23:18,398
My little papillons !

263
00:23:18,440 --> 00:23:20,943
[ Hysterical ] My butterflies , he killed them !

264
00:23:21,026 --> 00:23:22,194
No ... no !

265
00:23:22,277 --> 00:23:23,904
[ Cracking of neck ]

266
00:23:23,946 --> 00:23:26,281
You ... whining coward of a vampire

267
00:23:26,406 --> 00:23:30,035
who prowls killing rats and poodles ! You could 've finished us !

268
00:23:30,786 --> 00:23:32,204
You 've condemned me to Hell !

269
00:23:32,287 --> 00:23:33,914
I don 't know any Hell .

270
00:23:33,956 --> 00:23:35,749
[ Louis wailing ]

271
00:23:38,669 --> 00:23:40,921
LESTAT : [ Chuckling ] That 's more like it !

272
00:23:40,963 --> 00:23:42,256
Anger ! Fury !

273
00:23:42,464 --> 00:23:44,424
That 's why I chose you !

274
00:23:44,508 --> 00:23:46,468
[ Louis groaning and wailing ]

275
00:23:47,427 --> 00:23:48,846
[ Lestat chuckles ]

276
00:23:50,222 --> 00:23:52,808
But you can 't kill me , Louis .

277
00:23:57,271 --> 00:23:59,439
[ Louis breathes heavily ]

278
00:23:59,690 --> 00:24:00,941
Feed

279
00:24:01,483 --> 00:24:03,235
on what you will .

280
00:24:03,735 --> 00:24:05,571
Rats , chickens

281
00:24:05,696 --> 00:24:06,947
poodles .

282
00:24:08,073 --> 00:24:09,825
I 'll leave you to it

283
00:24:10,075 --> 00:24:12,244
and watch you come around .

284
00:24:12,494 --> 00:24:13,954
LESTAT : Remember :

285
00:24:13,996 --> 00:24:16,081
Life without me

286
00:24:16,248 --> 00:24:17,958
would be even more

287
00:24:18,083 --> 00:24:19,376
unbearable .

288
00:24:19,501 --> 00:24:20,586
[ Lestat chuckles ]

289
00:24:25,966 --> 00:24:27,885
[ Birds ' wings flutter ]

290
00:24:28,468 --> 00:24:30,220
[ Woman screaming ]

291
00:24:32,723 --> 00:24:34,391
[ Child crying ]

292
00:24:34,975 --> 00:24:36,977
[ Crickets chirping ]

293
00:24:37,019 --> 00:24:40,272
[ Rapid drumbeat , background ]

294
00:24:47,321 --> 00:24:49,281
[ Fire roars ]

295
00:24:54,620 --> 00:24:56,622
[ Chanting , drumbeat continues ]

296
00:25:18,519 --> 00:25:20,896
[ Softly ] Consider yourself lucky .

297
00:25:21,563 --> 00:25:24,775
In Paris , a vampire must be clever for many reasons .

298
00:25:25,776 --> 00:25:26,777
Paris ?

299
00:25:27,069 --> 00:25:29,905
Here all one needs is a pair of fangs .

300
00:25:30,822 --> 00:25:32,574
You came from Paris ?

301
00:25:32,783 --> 00:25:35,077
As did the one who made me .

302
00:25:36,828 --> 00:25:40,165
Tell me about him . You must 've learned something from him .

303
00:25:42,376 --> 00:25:44,795
I learned absolutely nothing .

304
00:25:45,796 --> 00:25:48,549
I wasn 't given a choice , remember ?

305
00:25:49,174 --> 00:25:51,802
You must know something about the meaning of it all .

306
00:25:51,844 --> 00:25:54,596
[ Yelling ] Why ? Why should I know these things ?

307
00:25:54,805 --> 00:25:56,306
Do you know them ?

308
00:25:56,431 --> 00:25:57,683
That noise

309
00:25:57,808 --> 00:25:59,852
it 's driving me mad !

310
00:26:00,060 --> 00:26:03,313
We 've been here for weeks with nothing but that noise !

311
00:26:03,438 --> 00:26:05,065
They know about us .

312
00:26:05,190 --> 00:26:09,111
They watch us dine on empty plates and drink from empty glasses .

313
00:26:09,862 --> 00:26:11,113
LESTAT : Come

314
00:26:11,196 --> 00:26:12,948
to New Orleans then .

315
00:26:13,365 --> 00:26:16,952
The Paris Opera 's in town . We can try some French

316
00:26:17,119 --> 00:26:18,453
cuisine .

317
00:26:19,121 --> 00:26:22,332
Forgive me if I have a lingering respect for life .

318
00:26:24,960 --> 00:26:27,379
You 'll soon run out of chickens , Louis .

319
00:26:31,842 --> 00:26:34,136
[ Dramatic , instrumental beat ]

320
00:26:36,847 --> 00:26:39,850
[ Flames roar , drumbeat intensifies ]

321
00:26:43,896 --> 00:26:45,439
[ Horse neighs ]

322
00:27:00,621 --> 00:27:01,872
Monsieur Louis ?

323
00:27:02,456 --> 00:27:04,750
YVETTE : You don 't want any supper ?

324
00:27:06,126 --> 00:27:07,377
No , ma chérie .

325
00:27:08,378 --> 00:27:10,506
We 're worried about you , Master .

326
00:27:12,674 --> 00:27:15,260
When is it that you go riding in the field ?

327
00:27:16,637 --> 00:27:19,640
And how long since you 've been to the slave quarter ?

328
00:27:22,643 --> 00:27:25,020
YVETTE : Everywhere there is death .

329
00:27:27,189 --> 00:27:29,650
Are you still our master at all ?

330
00:27:29,775 --> 00:27:31,693
That will be all , Yvette .

331
00:27:32,486 --> 00:27:35,531
YVETTE : I will not go unless you listen to me .

332
00:27:36,907 --> 00:27:39,451
You must send away this friend of yours .

333
00:27:40,536 --> 00:27:43,163
The slaves are all frightened of him

334
00:27:44,706 --> 00:27:46,917
and they are frightened of you .

335
00:27:52,256 --> 00:27:54,466
LOUIS : I 'm frightened of myself .

336
00:28:04,768 --> 00:28:06,311
[ Yvette gasps ]

337
00:28:12,734 --> 00:28:15,112
[ Yvette screams hysterically ]

338
00:28:16,238 --> 00:28:17,990
LOUIS : Hush !

339
00:28:20,033 --> 00:28:21,577
[ Smashing ]

340
00:28:25,247 --> 00:28:27,833
[ Scattered voices , flames roar ]

341
00:28:42,764 --> 00:28:44,516
Hear me now !

342
00:28:44,975 --> 00:28:46,977
This place is cursed !

343
00:28:47,102 --> 00:28:48,478
Damned !

344
00:28:48,770 --> 00:28:51,356
And , yes , your master is the Devil !

345
00:28:52,316 --> 00:28:55,027
LOUIS : Get out while you can ! You 're all free !

346
00:28:55,485 --> 00:28:56,862
Do you hear me ?

347
00:28:57,988 --> 00:28:59,031
Run !

348
00:28:59,156 --> 00:29:00,073
Run !

349
00:29:00,240 --> 00:29:02,284
Save yourselves !

350
00:29:12,920 --> 00:29:14,880
[ Mirror shatters ]

351
00:29:34,066 --> 00:29:36,026
[ Flames roar ]

352
00:29:50,832 --> 00:29:52,584
Perfect ! Perfect !

353
00:29:52,918 --> 00:29:56,421
Just burn the place ! Burn everything we own !

354
00:29:56,547 --> 00:29:59,132
Have us living in a field , like cattle !

355
00:29:59,216 --> 00:30:01,426
You thought you could have it all .

356
00:30:01,552 --> 00:30:03,053
Shut up , Louis !

357
00:30:04,346 --> 00:30:06,056
LESTAT : Come on !

358
00:30:06,056 --> 00:30:09,726
[ Dramatic , instrumental beat , background ]

359
00:30:26,660 --> 00:30:28,203
LOUIS : Where are we ?

360
00:30:28,996 --> 00:30:31,707
LESTAT : Where do you think , my idiot friend ?

361
00:30:31,874 --> 00:30:34,376
We 're in a nice , filthy cemetery .

362
00:30:35,210 --> 00:30:36,712
Are you happy ?

363
00:30:36,879 --> 00:30:39,381
LESTAT : Is this fitting ? Proper enough ?

364
00:30:40,090 --> 00:30:41,842
We belong in Hell .

365
00:30:42,009 --> 00:30:43,719
What if there is no Hell ?

366
00:30:43,886 --> 00:30:47,014
Or they don 't want us there ? Ever think of that ?

367
00:30:48,348 --> 00:30:50,851
LOUIS : But there was a Hell .

368
00:30:51,602 --> 00:30:54,605
And no matter where we moved to , I was in it .

369
00:30:54,646 --> 00:30:55,981
[ Thunder crackles ]

370
00:30:56,106 --> 00:30:58,859
We rented rooms on the waterfront of New Orleans .

371
00:30:58,901 --> 00:31:00,360
[ Women giggling ]

372
00:31:00,736 --> 00:31:02,863
WOMAN : Your skin is icy .

373
00:31:06,033 --> 00:31:08,410
[ Melody on piano , women giggle ]

374
00:31:23,717 --> 00:31:25,886
LESTAT : Your friend has no head for wine .

375
00:31:26,011 --> 00:31:28,180
[ Woman giggles ]

376
00:31:30,140 --> 00:31:31,767
Don 't worry .

377
00:31:32,226 --> 00:31:36,063
I can warm that cold skin of yours better than she can .

378
00:31:36,230 --> 00:31:38,023
LESTAT : Do you think so ?

379
00:31:39,066 --> 00:31:40,317
WOMAN : Why

380
00:31:40,567 --> 00:31:42,236
you 're warm now !

381
00:31:43,445 --> 00:31:45,656
But the price is high .

382
00:31:45,781 --> 00:31:48,283
Your pretty friend , I exhausted her .

383
00:31:52,079 --> 00:31:53,413
Soft .

384
00:31:55,290 --> 00:31:56,959
So soft .

385
00:31:58,669 --> 00:32:01,588
I can see you lying on a bed of satin .

386
00:32:02,589 --> 00:32:04,758
Such things you say .

387
00:32:06,260 --> 00:32:08,428
Do you know what manner of bed ?

388
00:32:12,683 --> 00:32:14,810
[ Woman breathes heavily ]

389
00:32:35,330 --> 00:32:37,332
LESTAT : Should we put out the light ?

390
00:32:37,457 --> 00:32:38,959
Uh-huh .

391
00:32:42,963 --> 00:32:45,215
LESTAT : And then put out the light .

392
00:32:45,257 --> 00:32:47,217
[ Woman walls ]

393
00:32:56,351 --> 00:32:58,312
[ Woman gasps ]

394
00:32:59,813 --> 00:33:02,774
LESTAT : But once I 've put out thy light

395
00:33:03,734 --> 00:33:04,985
I cannot

396
00:33:06,153 --> 00:33:08,739
give it vital breath again .

397
00:33:10,532 --> 00:33:12,534
Its needs must wither .

398
00:33:24,755 --> 00:33:26,256
For you , Louis .

399
00:33:26,381 --> 00:33:28,258
You can pretend it 's wine .

400
00:33:38,352 --> 00:33:39,603
She 's not dead !

401
00:33:39,686 --> 00:33:43,649
You 're in love with your mortal nature . You resist what can bring you peace .

402
00:33:43,774 --> 00:33:45,108
You call this peace ?

403
00:33:45,192 --> 00:33:48,570
We 're predators , whose all-seeing eyes give them detachment !

404
00:33:48,654 --> 00:33:51,823
LOUIS : The girl , Lestat ! LESTAT : Take her ! End that hunger !

405
00:33:51,907 --> 00:33:53,116
No !

406
00:33:53,825 --> 00:33:55,786
[ Woman screaming ]

407
00:33:59,706 --> 00:34:01,333
LESTAT : Now , my child .

408
00:34:03,210 --> 00:34:05,587
You 're tired , you want to sleep !

409
00:34:05,671 --> 00:34:07,214
[ Smashing ]

410
00:34:10,175 --> 00:34:11,927
[ Woman sobbing ]

411
00:34:14,054 --> 00:34:14,805
[ Thud ]

412
00:34:14,888 --> 00:34:16,807
WOMAN : [ Shrieking ] It 's a coffin !

413
00:34:16,890 --> 00:34:18,976
[ Wailing ] A coffin ! Let me out !

414
00:34:19,393 --> 00:34:20,894
WOMAN : I 'm not dead !

415
00:34:21,061 --> 00:34:25,607
It 's your coffin , enjoy it . Most of us never get to know what it feels like .

416
00:34:25,816 --> 00:34:27,317
Why do you do this ?

417
00:34:27,359 --> 00:34:32,072
I like to do it . I enjoy it . Take your aesthete 's taste to purer things .

418
00:34:32,322 --> 00:34:35,117
Kill them swiftly if you will , but do it !

419
00:34:35,325 --> 00:34:38,078
For do not doubt you are a killer , Louis !

420
00:34:40,455 --> 00:34:42,416
[ Banging and screaming ]

421
00:34:45,252 --> 00:34:47,921
LESTAT : What 's that ? WOMAN : It 's a coffin .

422
00:34:48,922 --> 00:34:50,966
So it is . You must be dead .

423
00:34:52,593 --> 00:34:54,344
I 'm not dead , am I ?

424
00:34:54,386 --> 00:34:55,971
LOUIS : No . You 're not dead .

425
00:34:56,096 --> 00:34:57,389
LESTAT : Not yet .

426
00:34:57,472 --> 00:34:59,141
Finish this now !

427
00:34:59,224 --> 00:35:00,475
LESTAT : You finish it !

428
00:35:00,601 --> 00:35:02,436
WOMAN : [ Sobbing ] Save me from him !

429
00:35:02,603 --> 00:35:03,604
Save me !

430
00:35:05,772 --> 00:35:07,149
You 'll let me go ?

431
00:35:07,649 --> 00:35:09,776
I can 't die like this !

432
00:35:10,152 --> 00:35:11,403
I need a priest .

433
00:35:11,486 --> 00:35:14,364
My friend is a priest . He 'll hear your sins before you die .

434
00:35:14,406 --> 00:35:16,491
Unless ... I make her one of us .

435
00:35:16,658 --> 00:35:17,618
No !

436
00:35:17,784 --> 00:35:21,663
Then take her , Louis , end her suffering ! End yours !

437
00:35:22,789 --> 00:35:23,790
No !

438
00:35:39,014 --> 00:35:41,183
[ Lestat breathes heavily ]

439
00:35:42,976 --> 00:35:44,394
LESTAT : Now

440
00:35:44,686 --> 00:35:46,396
are you happy ?

441
00:35:50,317 --> 00:35:51,693
My God !

442
00:35:53,654 --> 00:35:55,322
To think you

443
00:35:55,489 --> 00:35:57,824
are all I have to learn from .

444
00:36:01,328 --> 00:36:03,413
LESTAT : In the Old World

445
00:36:04,206 --> 00:36:06,917
they called it the " dark gift . "

446
00:36:09,545 --> 00:36:11,713
And I gave it to you .

447
00:36:15,509 --> 00:36:17,469
[ Sound of sewer water running ]

448
00:36:22,808 --> 00:36:24,768
[ Rat shrieks ]

449
00:36:33,694 --> 00:36:36,697
MAN : Don 't go that way , Monsieur . It 's the plague .

450
00:36:37,030 --> 00:36:40,242
MAN : Go back the way you came ! LOUIS : The way I came ...

451
00:36:40,325 --> 00:36:42,703
[ Fast-paced , dramatic music ]

452
00:36:55,799 --> 00:36:57,551
CLAUDIA : Mama .

453
00:37:20,782 --> 00:37:22,784
Please help us .

454
00:37:23,076 --> 00:37:25,495
Papa left us and didn 't come back .

455
00:37:33,295 --> 00:37:35,923
Please , wake Mama , Monsieur .

456
00:37:51,271 --> 00:37:53,815
[ Claudia cries and gasps ]

457
00:37:58,320 --> 00:37:59,863
[ Lestat giggles ]

458
00:38:02,950 --> 00:38:05,452
LESTAT : My philosopher . My martyr .

459
00:38:05,619 --> 00:38:08,038
" Never take a human life . "

460
00:38:09,790 --> 00:38:12,042
This calls for a celebration .

461
00:38:12,084 --> 00:38:14,086
[ Lestat sings cheerful melody ]

462
00:38:21,677 --> 00:38:24,471
LESTAT : There 's still life in the old lady yet .

463
00:38:27,850 --> 00:38:29,226
Come back !

464
00:38:29,476 --> 00:38:31,645
[ Shouting ] You are what you are !

465
00:38:33,647 --> 00:38:35,649
Merciful death .

466
00:38:36,483 --> 00:38:39,194
How you love your precious guilt .

467
00:38:48,704 --> 00:38:50,831
LOUIS : Her blood coursed in my veins

468
00:38:50,873 --> 00:38:52,833
sweeter than life itself .

469
00:38:52,916 --> 00:38:55,419
And , as it did , Lestat 's words made sense to me .

470
00:38:55,502 --> 00:38:57,421
I knew peace only when I killed .

471
00:38:57,504 --> 00:39:02,217
When I heard her heart in that terrible rhythm , I knew what peace could be .

472
00:39:02,509 --> 00:39:04,094
[ Sewer-water running ]

473
00:39:09,641 --> 00:39:11,852
[ Louis gasps ]

474
00:39:36,210 --> 00:39:40,214
LESTAT : All I need to find you , Louis , is follow the corpses of rats .

475
00:39:48,555 --> 00:39:50,432
Pain is terrible for you .

476
00:39:51,725 --> 00:39:55,437
You feel it like no other creature , because you 're a vampire .

477
00:39:57,147 --> 00:39:59,399
You don 't want it to go on .

478
00:39:59,483 --> 00:40:00,651
No .

479
00:40:03,737 --> 00:40:07,449
Then do what it is in your nature to do

480
00:40:07,658 --> 00:40:11,245
and you will feel as you felt with that child in your arms .

481
00:40:13,247 --> 00:40:15,457
LESTAT : Evil is a point of view .

482
00:40:16,083 --> 00:40:18,252
God kills indiscriminately

483
00:40:19,461 --> 00:40:21,296
and so shall we .

484
00:40:22,256 --> 00:40:27,094
For no creatures under God are as we are . None so like Him

485
00:40:27,177 --> 00:40:28,554
as ourselves .

486
00:40:30,931 --> 00:40:33,183
I have a gift for you .

487
00:40:34,560 --> 00:40:35,936
Come .

488
00:40:39,815 --> 00:40:40,816
Please .

489
00:40:54,121 --> 00:40:56,874
LESTAT : She 's here . LOUIS : What are you saying ?

490
00:40:57,958 --> 00:40:59,501
You need

491
00:41:01,545 --> 00:41:03,755
more congenial than mine .

492
00:41:08,844 --> 00:41:11,096
LESTAT : Remember how you wanted her ?

493
00:41:11,847 --> 00:41:13,473
The taste of her ?

494
00:41:15,350 --> 00:41:17,477
I thought I 'd killed her .

495
00:41:20,480 --> 00:41:22,024
LESTAT : Don 't worry .

496
00:41:23,650 --> 00:41:25,485
Your conscience is clear .

497
00:41:38,498 --> 00:41:39,875
LESTAT : Claudia .

498
00:41:46,757 --> 00:41:48,258
Listen to me .

499
00:41:49,009 --> 00:41:50,886
You 're ill , my precious .

500
00:41:51,386 --> 00:41:55,349
And I 'm going to give you what you need to get well .

501
00:42:07,778 --> 00:42:08,904
No .

502
00:42:09,696 --> 00:42:11,532
You want her to die then ?

503
00:42:26,713 --> 00:42:28,423
LESTAT : That 's it . Yes .

504
00:42:36,056 --> 00:42:39,726
[ Simulated heartbeat rhythm , Lestat breathes heavily ]

505
00:42:42,604 --> 00:42:43,856
LESTAT : Stop !

506
00:42:46,233 --> 00:42:47,609
Stop !

507
00:42:48,110 --> 00:42:49,236
Enough !

508
00:42:49,820 --> 00:42:51,947
[ Lestat breathes rapidly ]

509
00:43:28,859 --> 00:43:30,360
I want some more .

510
00:43:30,485 --> 00:43:32,988
LESTAT : Of course you want more .

511
00:43:36,450 --> 00:43:37,993
[ Bells ring ]

512
00:43:40,746 --> 00:43:43,624
MAID : Vous m 'avez appelée , Monsieur ?

513
00:43:43,665 --> 00:43:46,043
Ah , quelle belle enfant !

514
00:44:02,684 --> 00:44:04,520
LESTAT : Gently , chérie .

515
00:44:05,521 --> 00:44:07,523
They 're so innocent .

516
00:44:08,899 --> 00:44:11,026
They must not be made to suffer .

517
00:44:12,319 --> 00:44:13,529
Good .

518
00:44:15,822 --> 00:44:16,990
LESTAT : Yes .

519
00:44:17,199 --> 00:44:18,659
All right , now .

520
00:44:18,825 --> 00:44:19,993
Stop .

521
00:44:20,077 --> 00:44:22,162
Aah ... aah ... aah !

522
00:44:22,496 --> 00:44:24,540
That 's enough , chérie .

523
00:44:24,957 --> 00:44:27,501
You must stop before the heart stops .

524
00:44:28,794 --> 00:44:30,003
I want more .

525
00:44:30,170 --> 00:44:31,421
LESTAT : I know .

526
00:44:31,713 --> 00:44:33,924
But it 's best in the beginning

527
00:44:34,049 --> 00:44:36,844
lest the Death takes you down with it .

528
00:44:37,845 --> 00:44:40,055
You 've done very well . Look at you .

529
00:44:40,347 --> 00:44:42,683
Not a drop split . Very good .

530
00:44:45,435 --> 00:44:46,937
Where is Mama ?

531
00:44:50,357 --> 00:44:52,192
Mama 's gone

532
00:44:52,526 --> 00:44:55,863
to Heaven , chérie , like that sweet lady right there .

533
00:44:57,197 --> 00:44:58,866
They all go to Heaven .

534
00:44:59,366 --> 00:45:00,951
All but us .

535
00:45:02,077 --> 00:45:04,454
Do you want to frighten our daughter ?

536
00:45:04,580 --> 00:45:06,206
I 'm not your daughter .

537
00:45:06,248 --> 00:45:07,875
Oh , yes , you are .

538
00:45:08,458 --> 00:45:10,711
You 're my and Louis ' daughter now .

539
00:45:11,044 --> 00:45:13,755
You see , Louis was going to leave us .

540
00:45:14,882 --> 00:45:16,967
LESTAT : He was going to go away .

541
00:45:17,718 --> 00:45:19,219
But now he 's not .

542
00:45:20,220 --> 00:45:21,972
Now he 's going to stay

543
00:45:22,097 --> 00:45:23,974
and make you happy .

544
00:45:26,268 --> 00:45:27,394
Louis .

545
00:45:33,275 --> 00:45:34,985
You fiend .

546
00:45:35,235 --> 00:45:37,029
One happy family .

547
00:45:46,997 --> 00:45:49,041
He did it to make you stay with him ?

548
00:45:49,124 --> 00:45:50,584
Perhaps .

549
00:45:50,751 --> 00:45:55,005
He knew me . He knew I would love her more than the waking world .

550
00:45:56,757 --> 00:45:58,926
LOUIS : But there was more to it .

551
00:45:59,259 --> 00:46:02,804
He lavished affection on her , there is no doubt about that .

552
00:46:03,931 --> 00:46:08,143
Perhaps , in the end , he did it because he was lonely too .

553
00:46:08,268 --> 00:46:11,021
SEAMSTRESS : I need more light . LESTAT : She needs more light .

554
00:46:11,104 --> 00:46:13,273
SEAMSTRESS : I 'll go blind without another lamp .

555
00:46:13,315 --> 00:46:14,441
LESTAT : She 'll go blind .

556
00:46:14,525 --> 00:46:16,568
SEAMSTRESS : Or let me fit this child during the day .

557
00:46:16,652 --> 00:46:20,447
LESTAT : Well , I am afraid , Madame , that my days are sacrosanct .

558
00:46:21,823 --> 00:46:24,076
LOUIS : A little child , she was .

559
00:46:24,159 --> 00:46:26,119
But also a fierce killer

560
00:46:26,286 --> 00:46:31,166
now capable of the ruthless pursuit of blood with all a child 's demanding .

561
00:46:32,835 --> 00:46:34,628
Let me kiss it better .

562
00:46:40,050 --> 00:46:41,802
[ Seamstress gasps ]

563
00:46:44,972 --> 00:46:46,723
Claudia ! Claudia !

564
00:46:48,559 --> 00:46:49,643
Now

565
00:46:50,185 --> 00:46:53,856
who will we get to finish your dress ? Be practical !

566
00:46:54,064 --> 00:46:56,316
Remember , never in our home !

567
00:46:57,192 --> 00:46:59,987
LOUIS : She slept in my coffin at first

568
00:47:00,153 --> 00:47:03,073
curling her little fingers around my hair

569
00:47:03,198 --> 00:47:05,951
till the day when she wanted her own coffin .

570
00:47:13,584 --> 00:47:16,003
But still , whenever she awoke

571
00:47:16,211 --> 00:47:18,172
she would crawl into mine .

572
00:47:29,224 --> 00:47:33,145
They died fast in those days , before , she learned to play with them

573
00:47:33,228 --> 00:47:36,648
to delay the moment till she had taken what she wanted .

574
00:47:37,232 --> 00:47:39,401
[ Buggy rattles ]

575
00:47:44,740 --> 00:47:46,283
[ Claudia cries ]

576
00:47:50,412 --> 00:47:52,706
WOMAN : Why are you crying , child ?

577
00:47:52,873 --> 00:47:54,499
Are you lost , my love ?

578
00:47:54,875 --> 00:47:56,251
Mama !

579
00:47:57,419 --> 00:47:59,296
Hush , now , don 't cry .

580
00:47:59,505 --> 00:48:00,547
We 'll find her .

581
00:48:00,631 --> 00:48:03,217
CLAUDIA : Mama ! WOMAN : Oh , mon chère .

582
00:48:05,636 --> 00:48:07,679
[ Piano playing classical melody ]

583
00:48:08,013 --> 00:48:11,767
Mind the thumb , girl . Mind the thumb . That little digit .

584
00:48:26,031 --> 00:48:28,659
They 're expensive , my dear .

585
00:48:29,952 --> 00:48:33,455
Maybe too expensive for a young girl like you .

586
00:48:47,219 --> 00:48:49,346
Claudia ! What have we told you !

587
00:48:50,180 --> 00:48:51,932
Never in the house .

588
00:48:54,184 --> 00:48:55,686
Give me some room .

589
00:48:56,979 --> 00:48:58,814
LOUIS : To me , she was a child .

590
00:48:58,939 --> 00:49:01,316
But to Lestat , a pupil

591
00:49:01,692 --> 00:49:04,987
an infant prodigy with a lust for killing like his own .

592
00:49:05,571 --> 00:49:08,699
Together , they finished off whole families .

593
00:49:08,740 --> 00:49:10,826
[ Piano playing classical melody ]

594
00:49:12,703 --> 00:49:14,454
[ Applause ]

595
00:49:15,706 --> 00:49:17,457
Wonderful , wonderful .

596
00:49:17,708 --> 00:49:20,460
Now try something on a more somber note .

597
00:49:25,966 --> 00:49:29,553
[ Piano playing transforms into orchestral music ]

598
00:49:34,099 --> 00:49:37,227
LOUIS : Time can pass quickly for mortals when they 're happy .

599
00:49:37,269 --> 00:49:39,354
With us , it was the same .

600
00:49:39,521 --> 00:49:42,858
The years flew by like minutes . The city grew .

601
00:49:43,025 --> 00:49:45,235
Sailboats gave way to steamships

602
00:49:45,277 --> 00:49:49,156
disgorging an endless menu of magnificent strangers .

603
00:49:50,115 --> 00:49:52,326
A new world had sprung up around us .

604
00:49:52,492 --> 00:49:54,786
And we were all Americans now .

605
00:49:54,870 --> 00:49:56,413
[ Bells ring ]

606
00:50:00,083 --> 00:50:01,835
[ Fog horn blows ]

607
00:50:03,003 --> 00:50:05,172
LESTAT : This filthy modern tide !

608
00:50:05,297 --> 00:50:09,760
What I wouldn 't give for a drop of old-fashioned Creole blood !

609
00:50:09,885 --> 00:50:12,262
LOUIS : Yankees are not to your taste ?

610
00:50:12,513 --> 00:50:16,016
Their Democratic flavor doesn 't suit my palate , Louis .

611
00:50:16,517 --> 00:50:18,310
[ Woman singing melody ]

612
00:50:34,576 --> 00:50:36,578
Now that is pure Creole .

613
00:50:39,915 --> 00:50:42,584
LESTAT : Trust Claudia to have found her .

614
00:50:45,295 --> 00:50:46,547
LESTAT : What ?

615
00:50:47,089 --> 00:50:48,590
Don 't you want her ?

616
00:50:48,966 --> 00:50:50,801
I want to be her .

617
00:50:53,345 --> 00:50:54,346
Can I ?

618
00:50:54,596 --> 00:50:56,723
CLAUDIA : Be like her one day ?

619
00:51:00,435 --> 00:51:04,064
More melancholy nonsense . You grow more like Louis daily !

620
00:51:04,189 --> 00:51:06,066
Soon you 'll be eating rats .

621
00:51:07,568 --> 00:51:10,445
Rats ? When did you eat rats , Louis ?

622
00:51:11,321 --> 00:51:13,323
It was a long , long time ago .

623
00:51:13,448 --> 00:51:14,908
Before you were born .

624
00:51:14,992 --> 00:51:16,243
[ Louis slurps ]

625
00:51:16,326 --> 00:51:18,620
LOUIS : And I don 't recommend them .

626
00:51:20,956 --> 00:51:25,586
LOUIS : Thirty years had passed , yet her body remained that of an eternal child .

627
00:51:26,461 --> 00:51:30,966
Her eyes alone told the story of her age , staring from under her curls

628
00:51:31,133 --> 00:51:32,593
with a questioning

629
00:51:32,634 --> 00:51:35,137
that would one day need an answer .

630
00:51:45,105 --> 00:51:46,398
Another doll .

631
00:51:46,607 --> 00:51:48,942
CLAUDIA : I have dozens , you realize .

632
00:51:49,651 --> 00:51:51,862
I thought you could use one more .

633
00:51:52,654 --> 00:51:54,865
CLAUDIA : Why always on this night ?

634
00:51:55,866 --> 00:51:57,409
What do you mean ?

635
00:51:57,618 --> 00:52:00,746
You always give me a doll on the same night of the year .

636
00:52:02,456 --> 00:52:04,166
I didn 't realize .

637
00:52:04,374 --> 00:52:06,376
CLAUDIA : Is this my birthday ?

638
00:52:10,631 --> 00:52:12,633
You dress me like a doll .

639
00:52:13,133 --> 00:52:15,010
You make my hair like a doll .

640
00:52:15,135 --> 00:52:16,136
Why ?

641
00:52:16,678 --> 00:52:19,890
Some of these , Claudia , are so old

642
00:52:20,432 --> 00:52:21,683
tattered .

643
00:52:22,893 --> 00:52:25,771
- You should throw them away . - I will , then !

644
00:52:31,985 --> 00:52:33,320
Claudia !

645
00:52:39,034 --> 00:52:40,702
LESTAT : What have you done ?

646
00:52:40,786 --> 00:52:42,788
[ Screaming ] What you told me to do !

647
00:52:42,913 --> 00:52:45,916
LOUIS : You leave a corpse here to rot ? CLAUDIA : I wanted her !

648
00:52:46,041 --> 00:52:48,460
CLAUDIA : I wanted to be her ! LESTAT : She 's mad !

649
00:52:48,544 --> 00:52:51,421
LESTAT : She pollutes the very house we live in !

650
00:52:52,214 --> 00:52:55,175
CLAUDIA : Do you want me to be a doll forever ?

651
00:52:56,301 --> 00:52:57,553
LOUIS : Don 't !

652
00:52:57,678 --> 00:52:59,805
Why not ? Can 't I change

653
00:52:59,972 --> 00:53:01,598
like everyone else ?

654
00:53:22,035 --> 00:53:23,787
[ Claudia screaming ]

655
00:53:27,833 --> 00:53:30,210
[ Shrieking ] Which one of you did it ?

656
00:53:30,335 --> 00:53:32,296
Which one of you did it ?

657
00:53:32,504 --> 00:53:35,257
CLAUDIA : Which one of you made me the way I am ?

658
00:53:35,340 --> 00:53:36,758
What you are ?

659
00:53:36,967 --> 00:53:40,345
A vampire gone insane , that pollutes its own bed !

660
00:53:40,512 --> 00:53:42,306
And if I cut my hair again ?

661
00:53:42,472 --> 00:53:44,349
It will grow back again .

662
00:53:44,474 --> 00:53:46,226
CLAUDIA : But it wasn 't always so !

663
00:53:46,268 --> 00:53:49,021
I had a mother once . And Louis , he had a wife .

664
00:53:49,479 --> 00:53:51,356
He was mortal , same as she .

665
00:53:51,523 --> 00:53:53,525
CLAUDIA : And so was I ! LOUIS : Claudia !

666
00:53:53,609 --> 00:53:55,277
You made us what we are !

667
00:53:55,527 --> 00:53:56,862
Stop her .

668
00:53:56,987 --> 00:53:58,572
Did you do it to me ?

669
00:54:05,621 --> 00:54:07,039
How did you do it ?

670
00:54:07,247 --> 00:54:09,374
And why should I tell you ?

671
00:54:10,042 --> 00:54:12,002
It 's in my power .

672
00:54:12,586 --> 00:54:14,379
Why yours alone ?

673
00:54:14,546 --> 00:54:16,298
Tell me how it was done !

674
00:54:16,632 --> 00:54:17,883
Be glad

675
00:54:18,050 --> 00:54:20,135
I made you what you are .

676
00:54:21,512 --> 00:54:23,555
LESTAT : You 'd be dead now if I hadn 't .

677
00:54:23,639 --> 00:54:26,558
Like that damned corpse ! Now get rid of it !

678
00:54:26,892 --> 00:54:28,769
You get rid of it .

679
00:54:39,905 --> 00:54:41,406
Louis , why ?

680
00:54:41,657 --> 00:54:43,659
You 've got to tell me .

681
00:54:50,082 --> 00:54:52,042
LOUIS : You see the old woman ?

682
00:54:52,918 --> 00:54:54,920
That will never happen to you .

683
00:54:55,921 --> 00:54:57,798
You will never grow old .

684
00:54:58,423 --> 00:55:00,175
And you will never die .

685
00:55:01,802 --> 00:55:05,347
And it means something else too , doesn 't it ?

686
00:55:08,934 --> 00:55:11,353
I shall never , ever grow up .

687
00:55:16,358 --> 00:55:17,818
I hate him .

688
00:55:20,112 --> 00:55:23,574
Tell me how it came to be that I am this

689
00:55:24,366 --> 00:55:25,576
thing .

690
00:55:31,623 --> 00:55:34,626
LOUIS : For thirty years I 'd avoided that place .

691
00:55:36,128 --> 00:55:38,630
Yet I found my way back there

692
00:55:38,839 --> 00:55:41,592
with hardly an upward glance .

693
00:55:57,232 --> 00:55:58,483
You

694
00:55:58,650 --> 00:56:00,360
fed on me ?

695
00:56:00,736 --> 00:56:01,904
Yes .

696
00:56:03,739 --> 00:56:05,616
And he found me with you .

697
00:56:08,118 --> 00:56:11,163
Then he cut his wrist and fed you from him

698
00:56:11,496 --> 00:56:13,624
and you were a vampire then

699
00:56:13,874 --> 00:56:16,376
and have been every night thereafter .

700
00:56:19,671 --> 00:56:21,423
You both did it .

701
00:56:22,132 --> 00:56:23,884
I took your life .

702
00:56:26,386 --> 00:56:28,263
He gave you another one .

703
00:56:30,015 --> 00:56:31,892
And here it is .

704
00:56:32,017 --> 00:56:33,769
I hate you both .

705
00:56:44,154 --> 00:56:46,281
[ Dramatic , instrumental beat ]

706
00:56:46,406 --> 00:56:48,200
LOUIS : I walked all night .

707
00:56:49,451 --> 00:56:51,787
I walked as I walked years before

708
00:56:51,954 --> 00:56:55,290
when my mind swam with guilt at the thought of killing .

709
00:56:56,542 --> 00:57:00,796
I thought of all the things I 'd done and couldn 't undo .

710
00:57:01,922 --> 00:57:04,299
And I longed for one second 's peace .

711
00:57:13,725 --> 00:57:16,061
CLAUDIA : Locked together in hatred .

712
00:57:20,816 --> 00:57:22,985
But I can 't hate you , Louis .

713
00:57:29,366 --> 00:57:31,326
Louis , my love .

714
00:57:33,203 --> 00:57:35,247
I was mortal till you

715
00:57:36,707 --> 00:57:39,084
gave me your immortal kiss .

716
00:57:40,752 --> 00:57:43,964
You became my mother and my father .

717
00:57:45,507 --> 00:57:47,843
And so I 'm yours forever .

718
00:57:50,012 --> 00:57:52,556
But now it 's time to end it , Louis .

719
00:57:54,099 --> 00:57:56,476
Now it 's time to leave him .

720
00:58:00,230 --> 00:58:02,274
He will never let us go .

721
00:58:04,026 --> 00:58:05,360
No .

722
00:58:14,119 --> 00:58:15,746
Really ?

723
00:58:18,123 --> 00:58:20,751
[ Piano playing classical music ]

724
00:58:27,257 --> 00:58:30,302
What is it now ? You irritate me . Your very presence

725
00:58:30,385 --> 00:58:31,553
irritates me !

726
00:58:31,637 --> 00:58:33,055
Does it ?

727
00:58:33,263 --> 00:58:36,558
I found someone who 'll be a vampire better than you both !

728
00:58:36,767 --> 00:58:38,852
Is that supposed to frighten me ?

729
00:58:39,561 --> 00:58:42,898
You 're spoiled , because you 're an only child .

730
00:58:43,524 --> 00:58:45,025
You need a brother .

731
00:58:45,776 --> 00:58:47,069
Or I do .

732
00:58:47,778 --> 00:58:49,571
I 'm weary of you both .

733
00:58:50,280 --> 00:58:53,283
I suppose we could people the world with vampires

734
00:58:53,325 --> 00:58:55,035
the three of us .

735
00:58:55,786 --> 00:58:57,329
Oh , not you

736
00:58:57,538 --> 00:58:59,289
my little Claudia .

737
00:58:59,790 --> 00:59:01,333
You 're a liar .

738
00:59:02,292 --> 00:59:04,336
But you upset my plans .

739
00:59:05,420 --> 00:59:07,297
What plans ?

740
00:59:08,173 --> 00:59:10,592
CLAUDIA : I came to make peace with you .

741
00:59:10,676 --> 00:59:13,345
Even though you 're the father of lies

742
00:59:14,054 --> 00:59:16,431
I want things to be as they were .

743
00:59:17,599 --> 00:59:19,351
Stop pestering me then .

744
00:59:22,938 --> 00:59:25,190
I must do more than that .

745
00:59:26,191 --> 00:59:28,235
I 've brought a present for you .

746
00:59:30,696 --> 00:59:32,197
Then I hope it 's

747
00:59:32,364 --> 00:59:34,074
a beautiful woman

748
00:59:34,575 --> 00:59:37,619
with endowments you 'll never possess .

749
00:59:41,081 --> 00:59:42,958
Why do you say such things ?

750
00:59:51,884 --> 00:59:53,844
You haven 't fed enough .

751
00:59:54,595 --> 00:59:56,471
I can tell by your color .

752
01:00:02,978 --> 01:00:04,479
Come and see .

753
01:00:21,205 --> 01:00:23,165
Don 't be angry with me .

754
01:00:23,290 --> 01:00:25,959
When I saw them , I knew they were for you .

755
01:00:27,377 --> 01:00:28,545
Drunk

756
01:00:29,379 --> 01:00:31,965
on brandywine . A thimbleful .

757
01:00:40,766 --> 01:00:42,476
You certainly have

758
01:00:42,684 --> 01:00:44,186
outdone yourself .

759
01:00:45,979 --> 01:00:48,565
I promise I 'll get rid of the bodies .

760
01:01:02,329 --> 01:01:04,206
We forgive each other then ?

761
01:01:05,666 --> 01:01:06,917
Yes .

762
01:01:20,556 --> 01:01:22,349
[ Lestat breathes heavily ]

763
01:01:22,432 --> 01:01:23,725
Absinthe ?

764
01:01:26,436 --> 01:01:28,355
You 've given them absinthe ?

765
01:01:28,730 --> 01:01:29,731
No .

766
01:01:30,107 --> 01:01:31,233
Laudanum .

767
01:01:32,734 --> 01:01:33,819
Laudanum .

768
01:01:33,986 --> 01:01:35,028
Yes .

769
01:01:35,612 --> 01:01:37,781
It killed them , unfortunately .

770
01:01:38,448 --> 01:01:40,534
But it keeps the blood warm .

771
01:01:44,788 --> 01:01:46,623
LESTAT : You let me drink

772
01:01:48,250 --> 01:01:49,877
dead blood ?

773
01:01:50,377 --> 01:01:52,129
You let me

774
01:01:52,296 --> 01:01:53,505
drink ...

775
01:01:54,548 --> 01:01:56,758
One lesson you taught me

776
01:01:56,884 --> 01:01:58,844
never drink from the dead .

777
01:01:59,970 --> 01:02:01,221
Louis !

778
01:02:01,763 --> 01:02:03,765
[ Gasping ] Put me in my coffin .

779
01:02:03,974 --> 01:02:05,475
Put me in my coffin .

780
01:02:05,559 --> 01:02:08,478
CLAUDIA : [ Screaming ] I 'll put you in your coffin !

781
01:02:12,566 --> 01:02:13,567
My God !

782
01:02:13,650 --> 01:02:15,819
[ Lestat gasps ]

783
01:02:20,616 --> 01:02:22,159
[ Choking sounds ]

784
01:02:29,249 --> 01:02:31,001
Louis

785
01:02:31,084 --> 01:02:32,586
lift me up !

786
01:02:32,669 --> 01:02:34,838
[ Lestat takes short breaths ]

787
01:02:47,351 --> 01:02:50,020
CLAUDIA : Good night , sweet prince .

788
01:02:50,896 --> 01:02:54,608
May flights of devils wing you to your rest .

789
01:02:56,401 --> 01:02:58,111
Should we burn him ?

790
01:02:58,278 --> 01:02:59,530
Bury him ?

791
01:02:59,780 --> 01:03:01,615
What would he have liked ?

792
01:03:05,619 --> 01:03:06,787
The swamp ?

793
01:03:06,870 --> 01:03:09,456
[ Dramatic , instrumental music ]

794
01:03:10,791 --> 01:03:12,709
[ Sound of horses galloping ]

795
01:03:30,227 --> 01:03:32,229
He belongs with those reptiles .

796
01:03:34,565 --> 01:03:36,567
CLAUDIA : He deserved to die .

797
01:03:37,651 --> 01:03:40,571
Then perhaps so do we , every night of our lives .

798
01:03:43,991 --> 01:03:45,826
He was my maker .

799
01:03:46,827 --> 01:03:48,495
He gave me this life

800
01:03:48,662 --> 01:03:50,247
whatever it is .

801
01:03:53,333 --> 01:03:55,752
LOUIS : It shouldn 't have been this way .

802
01:03:55,836 --> 01:03:58,088
CLAUDIA : I did it for us .

803
01:03:58,755 --> 01:04:00,674
So we could be free .

804
01:04:07,014 --> 01:04:08,348
You missed him ?

805
01:04:10,017 --> 01:04:11,602
He was all I knew .

806
01:04:11,768 --> 01:04:13,478
It 's as simple as that .

807
01:04:14,521 --> 01:04:17,357
We were like two orphans learning to live again .

808
01:04:19,610 --> 01:04:21,612
We booked a passage to Europe .

809
01:04:22,529 --> 01:04:25,199
LOUIS : Over the weeks , while waiting for the boat

810
01:04:25,282 --> 01:04:28,869
she studied the myths and legends of the Old World

811
01:04:29,036 --> 01:04:32,539
obsessed with the search of what she called " our kind . "

812
01:04:34,917 --> 01:04:36,668
[ Piano playing ]

813
01:04:36,960 --> 01:04:38,420
[ Knock on door ]

814
01:04:41,632 --> 01:04:43,550
[ Birds chirping ]

815
01:04:46,887 --> 01:04:48,639
LOUIS : Look who we forgot .

816
01:04:53,018 --> 01:04:54,728
Let 's set them free .

817
01:04:56,021 --> 01:04:58,065
CLAUDIA : Yes . LOUIS : Yes .

818
01:05:01,235 --> 01:05:02,569
[ Bells ring ]

819
01:05:02,653 --> 01:05:04,321
It 's the carriage .

820
01:05:07,282 --> 01:05:09,034
[ Bells ring again ]

821
01:05:33,433 --> 01:05:35,352
[ Gasping and grunting ]

822
01:05:35,602 --> 01:05:37,980
CLAUDIA : [ Screaming ] No , Louis !

823
01:05:45,279 --> 01:05:47,948
[ Piano playing melancholic , classical melody ]

824
01:05:50,826 --> 01:05:52,536
LESTAT : Listen , Louis

825
01:05:54,371 --> 01:05:55,956
there 's life

826
01:05:56,123 --> 01:05:58,292
in these old hands still .

827
01:06:01,128 --> 01:06:03,380
Not quite furioso .

828
01:06:06,133 --> 01:06:07,467
Moderato

829
01:06:08,719 --> 01:06:10,387
cantabile , perhaps .

830
01:06:10,846 --> 01:06:12,639
How could it be ?

831
01:06:12,890 --> 01:06:14,725
LESTAT : Ask the alligator .

832
01:06:15,475 --> 01:06:17,311
His blood helped .

833
01:06:19,646 --> 01:06:23,400
Then , on a diet of the blood of snakes

834
01:06:24,151 --> 01:06:25,319
toads

835
01:06:27,487 --> 01:06:29,907
and all the putrid life

836
01:06:30,157 --> 01:06:31,909
of the Mississippi

837
01:06:33,243 --> 01:06:34,620
slowly

838
01:06:35,829 --> 01:06:38,248
Lestat became something

839
01:06:38,498 --> 01:06:40,334
like himself again .

840
01:06:42,169 --> 01:06:43,754
Claudia ...

841
01:06:45,255 --> 01:06:46,757
You 've been

842
01:06:47,341 --> 01:06:48,926
a very

843
01:06:49,343 --> 01:06:50,636
very

844
01:06:50,761 --> 01:06:52,513
naughty little girl .

845
01:06:54,389 --> 01:06:56,350
[ Banging and gasping ]

846
01:07:01,897 --> 01:07:03,857
[ Claudia screams ]

847
01:07:06,693 --> 01:07:09,279
[ Lestat walls , flames roar ]

848
01:07:17,871 --> 01:07:20,666
[ Smashing and banging of furniture ]

849
01:07:37,683 --> 01:07:40,310
[ Chaos of voices in the streets ]

850
01:07:46,608 --> 01:07:49,194
[ Dramatic music intensifies , Lestat walls ]

851
01:07:54,741 --> 01:07:57,327
CLAUDIA : The ship is sailing without us !

852
01:08:16,513 --> 01:08:19,183
LOUIS : Though the fire seemed to spread

853
01:08:19,266 --> 01:08:23,228
I stood on that deck , fearful , he would come out again

854
01:08:23,353 --> 01:08:26,356
from the river like some monster , to destroy us .

855
01:08:27,524 --> 01:08:29,610
And all the while I thought ...

856
01:08:30,110 --> 01:08:31,236
" Lestat ...

857
01:08:31,445 --> 01:08:33,530
" ... we deserve your vengeance .

858
01:08:34,406 --> 01:08:36,533
" You gave me the ' dark gift ' ...

859
01:08:37,034 --> 01:08:41,246
" ... and I delivered you into the hands of Death for the second time . "

860
01:08:58,180 --> 01:09:01,683
Though the ship was blessedly free of rats

861
01:09:01,892 --> 01:09:05,646
a strange plague nonetheless struck its passengers .

862
01:09:07,147 --> 01:09:09,650
Claudia and I alone seemed immune .

863
01:09:11,193 --> 01:09:13,278
We kept to ourselves

864
01:09:13,445 --> 01:09:16,031
pondering the mystery of each other .

865
01:09:18,784 --> 01:09:20,536
We reached the Mediterranean .

866
01:09:20,661 --> 01:09:24,665
I wanted those waters to be blue ... but they were black ...

867
01:09:24,748 --> 01:09:26,542
LOUIS : ... night-time waters .

868
01:09:26,667 --> 01:09:28,669
And how I suffered then

869
01:09:29,044 --> 01:09:32,965
straining to recall the color that in my youth I took for granted .

870
01:09:39,304 --> 01:09:41,557
We searched village after village

871
01:09:41,723 --> 01:09:43,225
ruin after ruin

872
01:09:43,308 --> 01:09:45,185
country after country .

873
01:09:45,477 --> 01:09:47,563
And always we found nothing .

874
01:09:49,982 --> 01:09:53,485
I began to believe we were the only ones .

875
01:09:54,945 --> 01:09:57,739
There was a strange comfort in that thought .

876
01:09:58,073 --> 01:10:01,827
For what could the damned really have to say to the damned ?

877
01:10:03,704 --> 01:10:05,080
You found nothing ?

878
01:10:05,205 --> 01:10:06,582
Peasant rumors

879
01:10:07,082 --> 01:10:09,126
superstitions about garlic

880
01:10:09,334 --> 01:10:10,586
crosses

881
01:10:10,752 --> 01:10:12,963
the old stake in the heart .

882
01:10:14,006 --> 01:10:15,966
But one of our kind ?

883
01:10:16,091 --> 01:10:17,467
Not a whisper .

884
01:10:19,261 --> 01:10:23,473
There are no vampires in Transylvania ? No Count Dracula ?

885
01:10:23,599 --> 01:10:25,142
Fictions , my friend .

886
01:10:25,350 --> 01:10:27,728
The vulgar fictions of a demented Irishman .

887
01:10:29,271 --> 01:10:30,355
LOUIS : Paris

888
01:10:30,480 --> 01:10:32,107
September , 1870 .

889
01:10:33,233 --> 01:10:35,360
The city I 'd always dreamed of .

890
01:10:35,986 --> 01:10:40,115
I was Creole , after all , and Paris was the mother of New Orleans .

891
01:10:40,782 --> 01:10:44,244
A universe whole and entire unto herself .

892
01:10:44,286 --> 01:10:46,496
[ Orchestral music plays ]

893
01:11:19,071 --> 01:11:21,073
LOUIS : We were alive again .

894
01:11:21,281 --> 01:11:22,908
Just the two of us .

895
01:11:23,075 --> 01:11:27,412
And so euphoric was I that I yielded to her every desire .

896
01:11:31,542 --> 01:11:33,043
[ Footsteps ]

897
01:11:40,050 --> 01:11:41,552
LOUIS : So it was

898
01:11:41,677 --> 01:11:44,680
when I 'd given up the search for vampires

899
01:11:44,847 --> 01:11:47,182
that a vampire found me .

900
01:11:47,307 --> 01:11:48,851
[ Footsteps ]

901
01:11:55,065 --> 01:11:57,609
[ Church bells ring in distance ]

902
01:12:46,116 --> 01:12:48,911
[ Light , playful orchestral music ]

903
01:13:16,897 --> 01:13:18,273
Buffoon !

904
01:13:19,900 --> 01:13:21,318
ARMAND : Santiago !

905
01:13:28,951 --> 01:13:33,539
I 've searched the world for an immortal and this is what I find !

906
01:13:49,680 --> 01:13:52,266
LESTAT : Bring the petite beauty with you .

907
01:13:53,433 --> 01:13:54,977
No one will harm you .

908
01:13:55,060 --> 01:13:56,478
I won 't allow it .

909
01:13:59,231 --> 01:14:00,482
And

910
01:14:00,816 --> 01:14:02,526
remember my name :

911
01:14:04,486 --> 01:14:05,696
Armand .

912
01:14:13,829 --> 01:14:15,706
LOUIS : Remember what I told you .

913
01:14:15,831 --> 01:14:19,751
They have different powers . They 'll read your thoughts .

914
01:14:22,462 --> 01:14:24,214
[ Organ playing ]

915
01:14:32,514 --> 01:14:34,725
He 's the one , that 's the vampire .

916
01:14:36,268 --> 01:14:37,853
SANTIAGO : Two lovers

917
01:14:37,978 --> 01:14:41,023
wandering down their violet way

918
01:14:41,857 --> 01:14:45,027
whose passionate embraces , each to each

919
01:14:45,360 --> 01:14:47,905
permit no meditations on decay ...

920
01:14:49,740 --> 01:14:50,782
CROWD : Whoa !

921
01:14:50,866 --> 01:14:52,784
... until they find themselves

922
01:14:52,868 --> 01:14:54,494
within my reach !

923
01:14:54,786 --> 01:14:56,246
CROWD : Whoa !

924
01:14:56,288 --> 01:14:58,040
[ Santiago cackles ]

925
01:14:58,123 --> 01:14:59,791
[ Applause ]

926
01:15:01,001 --> 01:15:04,630
Vampires who pretend to be humans pretending to be vampires .

927
01:15:04,796 --> 01:15:06,381
How avant-garde .

928
01:15:06,548 --> 01:15:10,010
SANTIAGO : The monk whose soul with Heaven doth commune

929
01:15:10,886 --> 01:15:12,554
and spends his days

930
01:15:12,596 --> 01:15:15,140
in pious contemplation ...

931
01:15:15,265 --> 01:15:17,309
[ Male voice screaming ]

932
01:15:17,559 --> 01:15:20,354
... finds he will meet his Maker all too soon .

933
01:15:20,437 --> 01:15:22,356
[ Crowd laughs ]

934
01:15:22,523 --> 01:15:25,776
SANTIAGO : For all his prayers gets no remuneration .

935
01:15:30,906 --> 01:15:32,824
The lesson endeth here

936
01:15:33,283 --> 01:15:35,035
and it is this :

937
01:15:35,786 --> 01:15:39,581
Each one of you , my clammy hands must touch .

938
01:15:41,166 --> 01:15:44,670
SANTIAGO : Each one must bend his forehead to my kiss .

939
01:15:47,089 --> 01:15:48,423
But , hark !

940
01:15:48,966 --> 01:15:51,301
Methinks a mortal doth approach !

941
01:15:52,803 --> 01:15:54,429
[ Girl sobbing and screaming ]

942
01:15:54,555 --> 01:15:56,431
SANTIAGO : What have we here ?

943
01:15:57,182 --> 01:15:59,226
What beauty by my side ?

944
01:16:00,561 --> 01:16:02,855
A rose in bloom , a shrinking violet ?

945
01:16:02,938 --> 01:16:04,231
[ Girl shrieks ]

946
01:16:05,065 --> 01:16:07,818
Perhaps she has a mind to be my bride .

947
01:16:08,318 --> 01:16:10,696
Perhaps my lesson has not ended yet !

948
01:16:10,821 --> 01:16:12,656
[ Girl shrieks ]

949
01:16:13,198 --> 01:16:14,950
I don 't want to die !

950
01:16:15,117 --> 01:16:17,828
SANTIAGO : But Death we are and have always been .

951
01:16:17,870 --> 01:16:19,454
GIRL : Someone help me !

952
01:16:19,580 --> 01:16:21,123
Please !

953
01:16:21,206 --> 01:16:23,584
[ Girl sobbing and wailing ]

954
01:16:30,591 --> 01:16:33,218
GIRL : What have I done ? SANTIAGO : We all die !

955
01:16:33,594 --> 01:16:34,636
GIRL : But I 'm young !

956
01:16:34,720 --> 01:16:39,141
SANTIAGO : Death is no respecter of age ! It can come any time , any place .

957
01:16:52,696 --> 01:16:55,616
SANTIAGO : Just as this flesh is pink now

958
01:16:55,866 --> 01:16:58,994
so it will turn gray and wrinkle with age .

959
01:16:59,036 --> 01:17:01,163
GIRL : [ Shrieking ] Let me live ! I don 't care !

960
01:17:01,246 --> 01:17:03,916
Then why should you care if you die now ?

961
01:17:03,999 --> 01:17:07,878
And suppose Death had a heart to love and to release you ?

962
01:17:08,378 --> 01:17:10,506
To whom would he turn his passion ?

963
01:17:10,672 --> 01:17:13,509
Would you choose a person from the crowd there ?

964
01:17:13,675 --> 01:17:15,511
A person to suffer as you do ?

965
01:17:15,636 --> 01:17:17,429
Monsieur Vampire , take me !

966
01:17:17,638 --> 01:17:19,515
I adore you !

967
01:17:20,015 --> 01:17:22,434
SANTIAGO : You wait your turn !

968
01:17:23,393 --> 01:17:24,895
Well ...

969
01:17:25,646 --> 01:17:29,650
Do you know what it means to be loved by Death ?

970
01:17:31,193 --> 01:17:33,904
To become our bride ?

971
01:17:33,946 --> 01:17:35,656
[ Explosion ]

972
01:18:16,864 --> 01:18:18,615
[ Girl cries ]

973
01:18:33,755 --> 01:18:35,257
No pain .

974
01:18:39,845 --> 01:18:41,346
No pain .

975
01:18:54,109 --> 01:18:55,527
Monstrous .

976
01:18:57,070 --> 01:18:59,239
[ Dramatic , instrumental music ]

977
01:19:45,077 --> 01:19:46,828
ARMAND : We live beneath .

978
01:19:47,329 --> 01:19:48,914
Let me show you .

979
01:19:54,920 --> 01:19:56,547
LOUIS : Monstrous .

980
01:19:57,422 --> 01:19:58,841
ARMAND : Yes .

981
01:19:59,842 --> 01:20:01,802
But very beautiful .

982
01:20:02,052 --> 01:20:03,804
[ Footsteps ]

983
01:20:23,073 --> 01:20:25,075
ARMAND : Welcome to my home .

984
01:20:40,090 --> 01:20:41,466
Try him .

985
01:20:53,687 --> 01:20:55,606
[ Crowd laughs ]

986
01:21:04,156 --> 01:21:05,866
Two vampires

987
01:21:06,909 --> 01:21:08,869
from the New World

988
01:21:12,873 --> 01:21:15,000
as all we love slowly rots

989
01:21:16,376 --> 01:21:18,128
and fades away .

990
01:21:18,921 --> 01:21:21,423
LOUIS : Are you the leader of this group ?

991
01:21:21,924 --> 01:21:23,884
If there were a leader

992
01:21:24,384 --> 01:21:26,011
I would be the one .

993
01:21:26,136 --> 01:21:29,640
LOUIS : So you have the answers ? ARMAND : So you have questions ?

994
01:21:31,683 --> 01:21:33,143
What are we ?

995
01:21:35,145 --> 01:21:36,480
Nothing

996
01:21:37,147 --> 01:21:39,024
if not vampires .

997
01:21:42,444 --> 01:21:44,488
LOUIS : Who made us what we are ?

998
01:21:45,030 --> 01:21:47,032
Surely you know the one who made you ?

999
01:21:47,157 --> 01:21:49,409
LOUIS : Yes , but the one who made him ?

1000
01:21:49,910 --> 01:21:51,161
The source

1001
01:21:51,203 --> 01:21:52,663
of all this

1002
01:21:53,539 --> 01:21:54,665
evil .

1003
01:21:56,792 --> 01:21:58,043
I understand .

1004
01:21:59,711 --> 01:22:01,922
ARMAND : I saw you in the theater .

1005
01:22:03,298 --> 01:22:05,217
Your suffering

1006
01:22:06,969 --> 01:22:09,054
your sympathy for that girl .

1007
01:22:10,931 --> 01:22:12,224
You die

1008
01:22:12,683 --> 01:22:14,059
when you kill .

1009
01:22:15,060 --> 01:22:18,814
You feel you deserve to die and you stint on nothing .

1010
01:22:20,566 --> 01:22:22,526
But does that make you evil ?

1011
01:22:23,569 --> 01:22:27,489
Since you comprehend what you call goodness , doesn 't that make you

1012
01:22:27,573 --> 01:22:28,699
good ?

1013
01:22:29,324 --> 01:22:31,076
Then there is nothing ?

1014
01:22:31,493 --> 01:22:33,203
ARMAND : Perhaps .

1015
01:22:34,830 --> 01:22:36,498
But perhaps

1016
01:22:38,250 --> 01:22:39,751
this

1017
01:22:40,210 --> 01:22:42,713
is the only real evil left .

1018
01:22:43,964 --> 01:22:46,258
Then God does not exist ?

1019
01:22:46,592 --> 01:22:48,886
I know nothing of God .

1020
01:22:49,887 --> 01:22:51,221
Or the Devil .

1021
01:22:51,722 --> 01:22:55,726
I have never seen a vision , nor learned a secret

1022
01:22:55,893 --> 01:22:58,896
that would damn or save my soul .

1023
01:23:00,731 --> 01:23:02,316
ARMAND : As far as I know

1024
01:23:02,399 --> 01:23:04,568
after 400 years

1025
01:23:05,360 --> 01:23:07,070
I am the oldest

1026
01:23:07,362 --> 01:23:09,239
living vampire

1027
01:23:09,406 --> 01:23:10,866
in the world .

1028
01:23:12,326 --> 01:23:14,870
Then it 's as I always feared .

1029
01:23:23,545 --> 01:23:25,422
You fear too much .

1030
01:23:27,758 --> 01:23:29,760
So much you make me fear ...

1031
01:23:35,098 --> 01:23:37,267
ARMAND : The one who made you

1032
01:23:37,601 --> 01:23:39,603
should have told you this .

1033
01:23:40,896 --> 01:23:43,774
The one who left the Old World for the New ...

1034
01:23:43,899 --> 01:23:45,359
LOUIS : He knew nothing .

1035
01:23:45,442 --> 01:23:47,110
Nor did he care .

1036
01:23:47,277 --> 01:23:48,278
Knew ?

1037
01:23:48,445 --> 01:23:49,780
Come , beloved .

1038
01:23:50,781 --> 01:23:52,908
It 's time we were on our way .

1039
01:23:53,033 --> 01:23:54,076
I 'm hungry

1040
01:23:54,159 --> 01:23:55,285
and the city awaits .

1041
01:23:57,287 --> 01:23:59,915
LOUIS : The place was empty as we left .

1042
01:24:00,123 --> 01:24:01,917
Silent as the grave .

1043
01:24:02,084 --> 01:24:05,587
And as we blundered through it , again came the thought :

1044
01:24:05,796 --> 01:24:07,923
" I have wronged Lestat .

1045
01:24:08,090 --> 01:24:10,342
" I have hated him for the wrong reasons . "

1046
01:24:10,425 --> 01:24:12,469
SANTIAGO : How did you wrong him ?

1047
01:24:14,304 --> 01:24:15,639
You said a name .

1048
01:24:15,931 --> 01:24:18,684
LOUIS : Yes , a name I don 't care to say again .

1049
01:24:18,809 --> 01:24:20,686
SANTIAGO : There is but one crime

1050
01:24:20,811 --> 01:24:22,813
among us vampires here .

1051
01:24:23,981 --> 01:24:27,484
It is the crime that means death to any vampire :

1052
01:24:29,152 --> 01:24:31,113
To kill your own kind .

1053
01:24:34,867 --> 01:24:37,119
LOUIS : Do you think I 'd let them harm you ?

1054
01:24:37,202 --> 01:24:38,579
CLAUDIA : No , you would not .

1055
01:24:38,662 --> 01:24:40,330
Danger holds you to me .

1056
01:24:40,497 --> 01:24:42,082
Love holds you to me .

1057
01:24:42,124 --> 01:24:43,750
CLAUDIA : Love ? LOUIS : Love .

1058
01:24:43,834 --> 01:24:46,962
You would leave me for Armand if he beckoned you .

1059
01:24:47,671 --> 01:24:48,839
Never .

1060
01:24:49,006 --> 01:24:52,593
CLAUDIA : He wants you as you want him . He 's been waiting for you .

1061
01:24:52,634 --> 01:24:54,970
He wants you as a companion .

1062
01:24:55,137 --> 01:24:57,014
He bides his time there .

1063
01:24:57,347 --> 01:25:00,100
CLAUDIA : He finds it as dull and lifeless as we do .

1064
01:25:00,142 --> 01:25:01,185
Perhaps .

1065
01:25:01,518 --> 01:25:05,522
Do you know what his soul said to me without saying a word ?

1066
01:25:06,690 --> 01:25:08,650
" Let him go , " he said .

1067
01:25:09,193 --> 01:25:10,861
" Let him go . "

1068
01:25:12,696 --> 01:25:14,990
Is that what I should do ?

1069
01:25:16,158 --> 01:25:17,868
Let you go ?

1070
01:25:18,869 --> 01:25:20,204
My father

1071
01:25:20,370 --> 01:25:21,872
my Louis

1072
01:25:21,997 --> 01:25:23,540
who made me ?

1073
01:25:25,375 --> 01:25:27,211
It will be all right .

1074
01:25:28,378 --> 01:25:30,380
You really believe that ?

1075
01:25:37,930 --> 01:25:39,473
SANTIAGO : The soldier

1076
01:25:39,556 --> 01:25:41,725
on returning from the war

1077
01:25:41,892 --> 01:25:45,562
thinks victory has ensured him against sorrow

1078
01:25:45,896 --> 01:25:47,898
till Death comes by

1079
01:25:48,232 --> 01:25:50,317
and chops him from his horse .

1080
01:25:51,026 --> 01:25:52,152
[ Cannon blast ]

1081
01:25:52,236 --> 01:25:54,404
[ Gasping and applause of audience ]

1082
01:25:56,532 --> 01:25:58,575
ARMAND : I was waiting for you .

1083
01:26:00,911 --> 01:26:02,412
LOUIS : Listen to me .

1084
01:26:04,748 --> 01:26:07,209
Claudia is very dear to me .

1085
01:26:07,543 --> 01:26:08,794
She 's my daughter .

1086
01:26:08,919 --> 01:26:10,420
ARMAND : Your lover .

1087
01:26:11,213 --> 01:26:12,673
LOUIS : No , my beloved .

1088
01:26:12,756 --> 01:26:14,216
My child .

1089
01:26:15,676 --> 01:26:18,053
ARMAND : You say so . You 're innocent .

1090
01:26:18,929 --> 01:26:20,931
She 's in danger , isn 't she ?

1091
01:26:20,973 --> 01:26:22,349
ARMAND : She is . LOUIS : Why ?

1092
01:26:22,432 --> 01:26:25,185
[ Light classical music on piano , background ]

1093
01:26:25,227 --> 01:26:27,563
ARMAND : I could give you reasons .

1094
01:26:28,730 --> 01:26:30,607
Her silence .

1095
01:26:31,441 --> 01:26:32,943
Her youth .

1096
01:26:34,444 --> 01:26:37,072
It 's forbidden to make one so young

1097
01:26:37,573 --> 01:26:39,449
so helpless

1098
01:26:39,783 --> 01:26:42,077
that cannot survive on its own .

1099
01:26:42,202 --> 01:26:43,829
LOUIS : Then blame the one who made her .

1100
01:26:43,954 --> 01:26:46,331
ARMAND : Did you kill this vampire who made you both ?

1101
01:26:46,456 --> 01:26:48,041
Is that why you won 't say his name ?

1102
01:26:48,125 --> 01:26:49,835
Santiago thinks you did .

1103
01:26:49,960 --> 01:26:53,463
LOUIS : We want no quarrel with him . ARMAND : It 's already begun .

1104
01:26:54,256 --> 01:26:55,966
If you want to save her ...

1105
01:26:56,091 --> 01:26:58,594
- ... send her away ! - Then I leave too .

1106
01:27:05,309 --> 01:27:06,810
ARMAND : So soon ?

1107
01:27:09,146 --> 01:27:12,482
Without any of those answers you so longed for ?

1108
01:27:12,816 --> 01:27:14,026
You said there are none .

1109
01:27:14,109 --> 01:27:16,320
But you asked the wrong questions .

1110
01:27:32,127 --> 01:27:33,504
Do you know

1111
01:27:34,171 --> 01:27:36,173
how few vampires

1112
01:27:37,174 --> 01:27:39,843
have the stamina for immortality ?

1113
01:27:41,803 --> 01:27:44,389
How quickly they perish of their own will .

1114
01:27:48,519 --> 01:27:50,145
The world

1115
01:27:50,812 --> 01:27:52,314
changes .

1116
01:27:54,316 --> 01:27:55,859
We do not .

1117
01:27:57,528 --> 01:27:59,530
Therein lies the irony

1118
01:27:59,655 --> 01:28:01,698
that finally kills us .

1119
01:28:02,199 --> 01:28:05,661
I need you to make contact with this age .

1120
01:28:06,328 --> 01:28:07,329
Me ?

1121
01:28:08,163 --> 01:28:09,831
Don 't you see ?

1122
01:28:10,666 --> 01:28:13,168
I 'm not the spirit of any age .

1123
01:28:14,044 --> 01:28:16,046
I 'm at odds with everything .

1124
01:28:16,171 --> 01:28:18,048
I always have been .

1125
01:28:19,550 --> 01:28:22,386
That is the very spirit of your age .

1126
01:28:23,720 --> 01:28:25,222
The heart of it .

1127
01:28:26,890 --> 01:28:28,684
Your fall

1128
01:28:28,851 --> 01:28:30,686
from grace

1129
01:28:30,853 --> 01:28:33,564
has been the fall of a century .

1130
01:28:34,690 --> 01:28:36,733
But the vampires in the theater ?

1131
01:28:38,569 --> 01:28:40,070
ARMAND : Decadent

1132
01:28:40,696 --> 01:28:42,197
useless .

1133
01:28:43,699 --> 01:28:45,909
They can 't reflect anything .

1134
01:28:46,577 --> 01:28:47,578
But

1135
01:28:48,078 --> 01:28:49,371
you do .

1136
01:28:51,582 --> 01:28:52,833
You reflect

1137
01:28:52,875 --> 01:28:54,585
its broken heart .

1138
01:29:07,097 --> 01:29:08,891
A vampire

1139
01:29:10,267 --> 01:29:12,227
with a human soul .

1140
01:29:13,437 --> 01:29:16,398
An immortal with a mortal 's passion .

1141
01:29:18,692 --> 01:29:19,902
You

1142
01:29:20,444 --> 01:29:21,778
are

1143
01:29:23,280 --> 01:29:25,282
beautiful , my friend .

1144
01:29:27,618 --> 01:29:30,746
Lestat must have wept when he made you .

1145
01:29:33,957 --> 01:29:35,626
You knew Lestat ?

1146
01:29:38,420 --> 01:29:39,755
Yes .

1147
01:29:40,964 --> 01:29:42,424
I knew him .

1148
01:29:44,259 --> 01:29:47,638
Knew him well enough not to mourn his passing .

1149
01:29:50,307 --> 01:29:52,935
LOUIS : I felt a kind of peace at last .

1150
01:29:53,477 --> 01:29:57,981
I had found the teacher which Lestat could never , I knew now , have been .

1151
01:29:58,774 --> 01:30:01,818
I knew knowledge would never be withheld by Armand .

1152
01:30:02,152 --> 01:30:05,656
It would pass through him as through a pane of glass .

1153
01:30:05,656 --> 01:30:07,658
[ Buggy rattles ]

1154
01:30:20,504 --> 01:30:22,047
CLAUDIA : Madeleine

1155
01:30:22,756 --> 01:30:24,424
Louis is shy .

1156
01:30:40,107 --> 01:30:41,358
Drink .

1157
01:30:41,441 --> 01:30:42,860
[ Louis sighs ]

1158
01:30:42,943 --> 01:30:44,194
Do it .

1159
01:30:44,361 --> 01:30:47,447
Because I cannot do it . I haven 't the strength .

1160
01:30:47,614 --> 01:30:51,952
- You saw to that when you made me . - You don 't know what you ask !

1161
01:30:54,204 --> 01:30:55,038
I have .

1162
01:30:55,122 --> 01:30:59,084
[ Yelling ] You have found your new companion ! You will make me mine !

1163
01:30:59,376 --> 01:31:01,044
How do we seem to you ?

1164
01:31:01,962 --> 01:31:03,714
Do you find us beautiful ?

1165
01:31:04,214 --> 01:31:05,549
Magical ?

1166
01:31:06,216 --> 01:31:11,054
Our white skin , our fierce eyes ? Do you know the thing you will become ?

1167
01:31:11,471 --> 01:31:14,016
CLAUDIA : Your evil is that you cannot be evil !

1168
01:31:14,141 --> 01:31:16,810
And I shall suffer for it no longer !

1169
01:31:17,144 --> 01:31:19,563
Don 't make me do this ! I cannot !

1170
01:31:19,980 --> 01:31:21,815
Yet , you could do it to me .

1171
01:31:22,149 --> 01:31:27,070
Snatching me from my mother 's hands , like two monsters in a fairy tale .

1172
01:31:27,738 --> 01:31:29,573
CLAUDIA : And now you weep !

1173
01:31:29,740 --> 01:31:32,659
I haven 't tears enough for what you 've done to me !

1174
01:31:32,910 --> 01:31:35,078
[ Shouting ] You give her to me , Louis !

1175
01:31:35,162 --> 01:31:37,664
Do this before you leave me !

1176
01:31:37,873 --> 01:31:39,750
[ Claudia weeps ]

1177
01:31:40,000 --> 01:31:41,084
Oh , God !

1178
01:31:41,835 --> 01:31:43,754
CLAUDIA : I love you still !

1179
01:31:44,171 --> 01:31:46,340
That 's the torment of it !

1180
01:31:47,341 --> 01:31:49,343
Who 'll care for me , my love

1181
01:31:49,927 --> 01:31:53,263
my dark angel , when you are gone ?

1182
01:31:59,603 --> 01:32:02,189
What do you think she is , Madeleine ?

1183
01:32:03,774 --> 01:32:05,192
LOUIS : A doll ?

1184
01:32:08,111 --> 01:32:10,030
A child who cannot die .

1185
01:32:11,281 --> 01:32:13,283
And the child who did die ?

1186
01:32:15,202 --> 01:32:16,912
MADELEINE : My daughter .

1187
01:33:11,091 --> 01:33:13,093
[ Madeleine shrieking ]

1188
01:33:13,385 --> 01:33:15,179
CLAUDIA : What 's happening to her ?

1189
01:33:15,262 --> 01:33:16,763
She 's dying .

1190
01:33:17,681 --> 01:33:19,683
It happened to you too

1191
01:33:20,017 --> 01:33:22,686
only you were too young to remember .

1192
01:33:24,605 --> 01:33:26,440
But if she dies ?

1193
01:33:27,441 --> 01:33:29,610
It 's only mortal death .

1194
01:33:33,197 --> 01:33:35,616
Bear me no ill will , my love .

1195
01:33:38,452 --> 01:33:40,370
We are now even .

1196
01:33:41,538 --> 01:33:43,123
What do you mean ?

1197
01:33:44,541 --> 01:33:47,878
What died in that room was not that woman .

1198
01:33:51,548 --> 01:33:53,383
What has died is the

1199
01:33:54,801 --> 01:33:56,803
last breath in me

1200
01:33:57,721 --> 01:33:59,556
that was human .

1201
01:34:03,810 --> 01:34:05,562
Yes , Father .

1202
01:34:06,563 --> 01:34:08,482
At last we are even .

1203
01:34:13,946 --> 01:34:16,907
PERFORMER : It 's time for justice , little one .

1204
01:34:16,990 --> 01:34:20,077
[ Dramatic , fast-paced music , screaming ]

1205
01:34:23,455 --> 01:34:25,415
[ Eerie laughter ]

1206
01:34:33,674 --> 01:34:36,927
Get me Armand . He wouldn 't stand for this .

1207
01:34:37,052 --> 01:34:38,846
Death for the others .

1208
01:34:39,513 --> 01:34:40,806
For you

1209
01:34:41,056 --> 01:34:43,350
eternity in a box .

1210
01:34:43,433 --> 01:34:44,476
[ Laughter ]

1211
01:34:44,560 --> 01:34:46,478
SANTIAGO : Walled in a dungeon .

1212
01:34:46,562 --> 01:34:49,231
Your only company will be your screams .

1213
01:34:50,065 --> 01:34:52,359
Perhaps it will take centuries .

1214
01:34:52,442 --> 01:34:53,944
[ Laughter ]

1215
01:34:53,986 --> 01:34:55,946
[ Shouting ] Take them !

1216
01:35:00,367 --> 01:35:02,536
LOUIS : [ Screaming ] Armand ! Armand !

1217
01:35:26,768 --> 01:35:29,146
[ Louis screaming and wailing ]

1218
01:35:33,400 --> 01:35:37,237
[ Music continues , vampires chatter and scream ]

1219
01:35:46,872 --> 01:35:50,501
[ Fierce laughter , Claudia screaming ]

1220
01:36:10,270 --> 01:36:12,147
SANTIAGO : Pleasant dreams .

1221
01:36:12,272 --> 01:36:13,899
[ AII cackle ]

1222
01:36:14,191 --> 01:36:16,109
LOUIS : No ! No !

1223
01:36:17,444 --> 01:36:18,862
Help !

1224
01:36:28,580 --> 01:36:30,541
[ Footsteps ]

1225
01:36:47,349 --> 01:36:49,309
[ Distorted sound effects ]

1226
01:36:54,690 --> 01:36:56,733
CLAUDIA : [ Sobbing ] Wake up !

1227
01:37:05,075 --> 01:37:08,704
[ Madeleine and Claudia screaming and gasping , echoes ]

1228
01:37:21,758 --> 01:37:23,927
[ Shrieking and raging ]

1229
01:37:26,346 --> 01:37:28,348
LOUIS : Claudia !

1230
01:37:41,278 --> 01:37:43,655
[ Fast-paced , instrumental music ]

1231
01:37:56,210 --> 01:37:58,795
[ Louis coughs and gasps for air ]

1232
01:38:02,966 --> 01:38:05,010
LOUIS : Where 's Claudia ?

1233
01:38:05,135 --> 01:38:07,721
Claudia . I cannot help her .

1234
01:38:08,222 --> 01:38:11,391
LOUIS : Where 's Claudia ? ARMAND : I can 't save her !

1235
01:38:12,726 --> 01:38:14,770
I will only risk losing you !

1236
01:38:16,980 --> 01:38:18,232
ARMAND : Don 't !

1237
01:38:19,066 --> 01:38:20,901
[ Footsteps ]

1238
01:38:44,174 --> 01:38:46,510
[ Sobbing and breathing heavily ]

1239
01:39:38,353 --> 01:39:40,731
[ Chorale music with organ , background ]

1240
01:40:06,006 --> 01:40:07,341
Come , Louis .

1241
01:40:08,759 --> 01:40:10,093
Not here .

1242
01:40:18,602 --> 01:40:20,896
INTERVIEWER : So a vampire can cry ?

1243
01:40:23,106 --> 01:40:24,274
Once

1244
01:40:24,608 --> 01:40:26,527
maybe twice , in eternity .

1245
01:40:28,570 --> 01:40:32,282
And maybe it was to quench those tears forever that I took such revenge .

1246
01:40:33,033 --> 01:40:35,369
[ Dramatic , instrumental beat ]

1247
01:41:19,621 --> 01:41:21,331
[ Flames roar ]

1248
01:41:29,339 --> 01:41:31,842
WOMAN : Stop him ! It 's burning !

1249
01:41:32,134 --> 01:41:34,094
[ Screaming ] Get him ! Stop him !

1250
01:41:34,136 --> 01:41:36,346
[ Chaos and screaming ]

1251
01:41:44,354 --> 01:41:45,606
[ Wailing echoes ]

1252
01:42:19,806 --> 01:42:21,141
Aaahh !

1253
01:42:21,225 --> 01:42:22,976
[ Evil cackling ]

1254
01:42:29,316 --> 01:42:31,527
[ Screaming and cackling ]

1255
01:43:00,556 --> 01:43:02,516
[ Screaming ]

1256
01:43:16,822 --> 01:43:18,615
[ Sound of hooves pounding ]

1257
01:43:19,366 --> 01:43:21,201
[ Buggy rattles ]

1258
01:43:22,536 --> 01:43:24,329
ARMAND : Louis !

1259
01:43:39,303 --> 01:43:42,222
LOUIS : You didn 't even warn them , did you ?

1260
01:43:43,599 --> 01:43:44,641
No .

1261
01:43:46,810 --> 01:43:49,104
And you knew what I would do .

1262
01:43:50,314 --> 01:43:51,648
I knew .

1263
01:43:52,107 --> 01:43:54,109
I rescued you , didn 't I ?

1264
01:43:54,276 --> 01:43:56,153
From the terrible dawn .

1265
01:44:00,490 --> 01:44:03,160
You were their leader . They trusted you .

1266
01:44:03,327 --> 01:44:04,286
No .

1267
01:44:05,495 --> 01:44:07,998
You made me see their failings , Louis .

1268
01:44:09,499 --> 01:44:10,792
They were

1269
01:44:10,876 --> 01:44:13,754
doomed , stuck in their decadent time .

1270
01:44:14,630 --> 01:44:17,174
They had forgotten the first lesson

1271
01:44:17,508 --> 01:44:19,510
that we must be powerful

1272
01:44:19,676 --> 01:44:21,011
beautiful

1273
01:44:21,136 --> 01:44:22,846
and without regret .

1274
01:44:23,805 --> 01:44:25,432
You can teach me this ?

1275
01:44:25,516 --> 01:44:27,017
Yes .

1276
01:44:27,184 --> 01:44:29,186
To be without regret ?

1277
01:44:31,355 --> 01:44:33,649
Then , what a pair we could make .

1278
01:44:36,360 --> 01:44:39,530
But what if it 's a lesson I don 't care to learn ?

1279
01:44:41,156 --> 01:44:42,157
What ?

1280
01:44:42,533 --> 01:44:45,202
What if all I have is my suffering ?

1281
01:44:45,536 --> 01:44:47,329
My regret ?

1282
01:44:48,956 --> 01:44:50,916
ARMAND : Don 't you want to lose it ?

1283
01:44:51,041 --> 01:44:53,293
LOUIS : So you can have that too ?

1284
01:44:53,877 --> 01:44:56,046
The heart that mourns her

1285
01:44:56,547 --> 01:44:58,674
whom you burnt to a cinder ?

1286
01:44:58,841 --> 01:45:00,467
ARMAND : I swear I didn 't ...

1287
01:45:00,551 --> 01:45:02,177
But I know you did .

1288
01:45:03,053 --> 01:45:04,346
I know

1289
01:45:05,806 --> 01:45:07,057
you

1290
01:45:07,683 --> 01:45:09,393
regret nothing .

1291
01:45:11,353 --> 01:45:12,896
You feel

1292
01:45:13,564 --> 01:45:14,690
nothing .

1293
01:45:16,692 --> 01:45:19,236
If that 's all I have left to learn

1294
01:45:20,863 --> 01:45:22,865
I can do that on my own .

1295
01:45:28,078 --> 01:45:29,162
Louis ...

1296
01:45:33,250 --> 01:45:34,668
I will die .

1297
01:45:34,751 --> 01:45:35,502
No .

1298
01:45:35,586 --> 01:45:37,087
You are dead .

1299
01:45:37,212 --> 01:45:39,923
And you want me to quicken you once more .

1300
01:45:42,259 --> 01:45:45,846
And as much as your invitation might appeal to me

1301
01:45:47,264 --> 01:45:49,099
I must regretfully

1302
01:45:49,433 --> 01:45:50,601
decline .

1303
01:46:03,447 --> 01:46:05,616
LOUIS : For years I wandered :

1304
01:46:05,741 --> 01:46:07,451
Italy , Greece

1305
01:46:08,118 --> 01:46:10,120
all the ancient lands .

1306
01:46:10,454 --> 01:46:12,915
But the world was a tomb to me

1307
01:46:13,123 --> 01:46:15,751
a graveyard full of broken statues .

1308
01:46:16,460 --> 01:46:20,047
And each of those statues resembled her face .

1309
01:46:25,969 --> 01:46:27,721
Then , out of curiosity

1310
01:46:27,888 --> 01:46:29,890
boredom , who knows what

1311
01:46:30,057 --> 01:46:31,642
I left the Old World

1312
01:46:31,725 --> 01:46:33,936
and came back to my America .

1313
01:46:37,147 --> 01:46:41,401
And there a mechanical wonder allowed me to see the sunrise

1314
01:46:41,568 --> 01:46:43,403
for the first time

1315
01:46:43,570 --> 01:46:45,405
in 200 years .

1316
01:46:46,657 --> 01:46:48,408
And what sunrises !

1317
01:46:49,076 --> 01:46:51,995
Seen as the human eye could never see them .

1318
01:46:52,829 --> 01:46:54,581
Silver at first

1319
01:46:55,332 --> 01:46:58,502
then , as the years progressed , in tones of purple

1320
01:46:58,585 --> 01:46:59,753
red

1321
01:46:59,920 --> 01:47:02,339
and my long-lost blue .

1322
01:47:07,010 --> 01:47:10,347
In the spring of 1988 , I returned to New Orleans .

1323
01:47:11,265 --> 01:47:14,852
And as soon as I smelled the air , I knew I was home .

1324
01:47:16,019 --> 01:47:17,354
It was rich

1325
01:47:17,521 --> 01:47:19,189
almost sweet

1326
01:47:19,356 --> 01:47:23,527
like the fragrance of jasmine and roses around our old courtyard .

1327
01:47:24,862 --> 01:47:29,366
I walked the streets savoring that long-lost perfume .

1328
01:47:29,449 --> 01:47:31,201
[ Sirens blare ]

1329
01:47:34,705 --> 01:47:36,874
LOUIS : And then on Prytania Street

1330
01:47:36,957 --> 01:47:40,043
only blocks from the Lafayette cemetery

1331
01:47:40,210 --> 01:47:42,379
I caught the scent of death .

1332
01:47:42,963 --> 01:47:45,465
And it wasn 't coming from the graves .

1333
01:47:47,050 --> 01:47:49,803
The scent grew stronger as I walked .

1334
01:47:49,970 --> 01:47:51,555
Old death .

1335
01:47:51,889 --> 01:47:54,558
A scent too faint for mortals to detect .

1336
01:48:27,841 --> 01:48:29,593
[ Footsteps ]

1337
01:48:32,262 --> 01:48:34,264
[ Gate creaks ]

1338
01:48:47,569 --> 01:48:49,530
[ Birds ' wings flutter ]

1339
01:49:18,141 --> 01:49:19,893
[ Footsteps ]

1340
01:49:26,692 --> 01:49:28,944
LESTAT : I 'm so glad you are here !

1341
01:49:29,611 --> 01:49:31,196
I 've dreamed

1342
01:49:32,072 --> 01:49:33,866
of this moment .

1343
01:49:35,450 --> 01:49:37,870
She never should have been one of

1344
01:49:38,453 --> 01:49:39,872
us .

1345
01:49:40,205 --> 01:49:42,207
That 's all past , Lestat .

1346
01:49:46,837 --> 01:49:48,338
LESTAT : Past .

1347
01:50:11,653 --> 01:50:13,864
Still beautiful , Louis .

1348
01:50:16,491 --> 01:50:18,994
You always were the strong one .

1349
01:50:21,163 --> 01:50:22,456
[ Banging ]

1350
01:50:23,165 --> 01:50:25,250
LOUIS : Don 't be frightened .

1351
01:50:28,921 --> 01:50:30,881
I mean you no harm .

1352
01:50:34,510 --> 01:50:37,012
LESTAT : You 've come home to me then ?

1353
01:50:41,141 --> 01:50:43,519
You remember how I was ?

1354
01:50:45,521 --> 01:50:47,189
The vampire

1355
01:50:47,397 --> 01:50:49,191
that I was ?

1356
01:50:50,275 --> 01:50:51,944
Yes , I remember .

1357
01:50:58,408 --> 01:50:59,535
No one

1358
01:50:59,701 --> 01:51:01,453
could refuse me

1359
01:51:02,955 --> 01:51:04,414
not even you .

1360
01:51:05,916 --> 01:51:07,417
I tried .

1361
01:51:08,043 --> 01:51:10,295
LESTAT : [ Softly ] Yes , you tried .

1362
01:51:11,213 --> 01:51:13,215
And the more you tried

1363
01:51:17,427 --> 01:51:19,513
the more I wanted you .

1364
01:51:21,765 --> 01:51:24,184
[ Lestat sighs deeply ]

1365
01:51:26,353 --> 01:51:28,730
[ Helicopter pelts overhead ]

1366
01:51:29,690 --> 01:51:32,234
LESTAT : [ Shrieking ] I can 't bear it .

1367
01:51:33,819 --> 01:51:35,445
LESTAT : Such lights

1368
01:51:36,822 --> 01:51:38,490
and that noise !

1369
01:51:40,075 --> 01:51:43,078
They make the night brighter than the day .

1370
01:51:51,461 --> 01:51:53,338
It 's false light .

1371
01:51:53,589 --> 01:51:55,340
It can 't harm you .

1372
01:52:06,602 --> 01:52:09,146
[ Whispering ] If you stay with me , Louis

1373
01:52:10,606 --> 01:52:12,566
I could venture out again .

1374
01:52:15,527 --> 01:52:17,613
Become the old Lestat .

1375
01:52:19,114 --> 01:52:20,991
I must leave now .

1376
01:52:49,061 --> 01:52:51,772
Whatever happened to Lestat , I do not know .

1377
01:52:53,065 --> 01:52:54,525
I go on

1378
01:52:54,650 --> 01:52:56,401
night after night .

1379
01:52:56,568 --> 01:52:59,071
I feed on those who cross my path .

1380
01:53:01,782 --> 01:53:05,035
But all my passion went with her golden hair .

1381
01:53:08,080 --> 01:53:11,083
LOUIS : I 'm a spirit of preternatural flesh .

1382
01:53:12,292 --> 01:53:13,919
Detached .

1383
01:53:14,795 --> 01:53:16,046
Unchangeable .

1384
01:53:18,966 --> 01:53:20,300
Empty .

1385
01:53:21,343 --> 01:53:22,928
INTERVIEWER : Empty ?

1386
01:53:23,053 --> 01:53:24,179
That 's it ?

1387
01:53:26,431 --> 01:53:28,350
No , it can 't end like that .

1388
01:53:29,935 --> 01:53:31,436
But it has .

1389
01:53:31,603 --> 01:53:33,355
There 's no more to tell .

1390
01:53:34,314 --> 01:53:38,986
There must be more to tell . You don 't understand yourself . You 're not empty .

1391
01:53:39,695 --> 01:53:42,948
What I wouldn 't give to be like you , to have your power

1392
01:53:43,073 --> 01:53:45,450
to have seen the things you have seen .

1393
01:53:45,576 --> 01:53:46,952
You haven 't been listening .

1394
01:53:47,077 --> 01:53:49,872
I have been listening . Your story is incredible .

1395
01:53:49,955 --> 01:53:51,999
- It 's amazing . - Do what you want with it .

1396
01:53:52,082 --> 01:53:54,501
Give it to others . Learn what you can .

1397
01:53:54,877 --> 01:53:58,589
There 's only one way I 'll truly learn and you know it .

1398
01:53:58,839 --> 01:54:01,383
You brought me here for a reason .

1399
01:54:01,633 --> 01:54:02,676
Didn 't you ?

1400
01:54:02,843 --> 01:54:04,595
What reason would that be ?

1401
01:54:04,720 --> 01:54:08,724
You want a companion . You want a link to the outside world . That 's me .

1402
01:54:08,891 --> 01:54:11,268
Take me . That 's what I want .

1403
01:54:11,351 --> 01:54:14,688
- I refuse to let it end like this . - God , I 've failed again .

1404
01:54:15,147 --> 01:54:19,193
INTERVIEWER : You haven 't failed . God has nothing to do with it .

1405
01:54:21,236 --> 01:54:22,654
Do you like this ?

1406
01:54:23,488 --> 01:54:26,408
Do you like being food for the immortals ?

1407
01:54:27,159 --> 01:54:28,493
Do you like dying ?

1408
01:54:28,619 --> 01:54:30,287
[ Gasping ] Stop !

1409
01:54:32,998 --> 01:54:35,167
[ Heavy breathing ]

1410
01:54:59,816 --> 01:55:01,568
[ Tires screeching ]

1411
01:55:02,819 --> 01:55:04,988
[ Horns honking ]

1412
01:55:08,909 --> 01:55:10,661
[ Heavy breathing ]

1413
01:55:21,421 --> 01:55:23,966
[ Dramatic , instrumental music ]

1414
01:55:26,176 --> 01:55:28,345
[ Short , rapid breathing ]

1415
01:55:37,437 --> 01:55:40,065
LOUIS ON TAPE : 1791 was the year it happened .

1416
01:55:40,190 --> 01:55:43,443
I was 24 . Younger than you are now .

1417
01:55:44,236 --> 01:55:47,322
But times were different then . I was a man at that age .

1418
01:55:47,447 --> 01:55:50,993
The master of a large plantation , just south of New Orleans .

1419
01:55:52,244 --> 01:55:54,830
I had lost my wife in childbirth .

1420
01:55:54,955 --> 01:55:56,248
Someone change my shorts .

1421
01:55:56,331 --> 01:55:59,960
LOUIS ON TAPE : She and the infant had been buried less than half a year .

1422
01:56:00,002 --> 01:56:00,752
It 's good stuff .

1423
01:56:00,836 --> 01:56:02,796
LOUIS ON TAPE : I would 've been happy to join them .

1424
01:56:02,880 --> 01:56:04,214
Good stuff .

1425
01:56:04,256 --> 01:56:05,716
[ Gasping ]

1426
01:56:07,593 --> 01:56:09,845
I assume I need no introduction .

1427
01:56:09,970 --> 01:56:11,263
[ Gasps ]

1428
01:56:11,346 --> 01:56:13,724
[ Tires screech ]

1429
01:56:16,268 --> 01:56:18,228
[ Smashing and banging ]

1430
01:56:24,359 --> 01:56:26,361
I feel better already .

1431
01:56:30,616 --> 01:56:33,493
LOUIS ON TAPE : Most of all , I longed for death .

1432
01:56:34,036 --> 01:56:35,621
I invited it .

1433
01:56:36,747 --> 01:56:39,082
A release from the pain of living .

1434
01:56:39,166 --> 01:56:41,043
Ah , Louis , Louis ...

1435
01:56:42,753 --> 01:56:44,505
Still whining .

1436
01:56:47,132 --> 01:56:48,634
Heard enough ?

1437
01:56:48,926 --> 01:56:52,137
I 've had to listen to that for centuries .

1438
01:56:54,139 --> 01:56:55,516
Don 't be afraid .

1439
01:56:58,018 --> 01:57:00,395
I 'm going to give you the choice

1440
01:57:01,313 --> 01:57:03,065
I never had .

